in-d889a2ccee70fe47,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=d889a2ccee70fe47,https://x.company/careers/8643805002,"Senior Staff Machine Learning Engineer, Tapestry",X Development,"Mountain View, CA, US",2026-07-22,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,262000.0,361000.0,USD,True,,,,-request@x.team,"Software EngineeringMountain View, CA (HQ)



**About Tapestry**


Tapestry is a team within Alphabet working to build the AI\-powered electric grid. We are tackling one of the world’s most important infrastructure challenges: helping the energy system become more visible, understandable, reliable, affordable, abundant, and clean.


Originally born at X, Alphabet’s moonshot factory, Tapestry brings together experts in energy, AI, software, engineering, and product to build tools that help the electricity ecosystem plan smarter, move faster, and operate more efficiently.


This is a global effort. Tapestry supports partners across the U.S., U.K., Chile, New Zealand, Australia, and Brazil as they work toward a cleaner, more resilient energy future.


Joining Tapestry means doing high\-impact work with a multidisciplinary team tackling a problem that matters at global scale. Learn more about our team and our mission here.


**About the role:**


You will serve as a foundational architect of Tapestry’s multi\-year machine learning strategy, bridging cutting\-edge AI research, the physics of continental\-scale power grids, and the development of production ML/AI systems. You will architect machine learning systems that advance grid planning, simulation, and asset intelligence at continental scale.


**How you will make 10X Impact**


* Own the technical roadmap and system architecture for Tapestry’s multimodal intelligence engines, scaling models across multimodal machine learning, graph neural networks, geospatial and remote\-sensing data, reinforcement learning for physical control systems, and multi\-turn agentic systems.
* Partner closely with Tapestry’s machine learning technical leads, Power Systems Scientists, Software Engineers, Product Managers, and global utility partners to translate complex, large\-scale grid data into actionable insights that improve grid planning, operations, and maintenance.
* Serve as a technical force multiplier across the engineering organization by mentoring senior and staff\-level engineers, establishing rigorous production standards, and aligning cross\-functional stakeholders around architectural direction.
* Advance the application of state\-of\-the\-art AI architectures—including physics\-informed neural networks and agentic AI—to solve highly constrained energy\-infrastructure challenges in production environments.
* Establish scalable architectural patterns and technical standards that improve the reliability, performance, and long\-term maintainability of Tapestry’s machine learning systems.
* Shape long\-term machine learning strategy through first\-principles thinking, rigorous technical analysis, and clear decision\-making across complex and evolving problem spaces.

**What you should have...**


* A Master’s degree or PhD in Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, Applied Mathematics, or a related quantitative field, or equivalent practical experience.
* 10\+ years of professional experience building, training, and deploying large\-scale machine learning systems in production, with deep proficiency in modern frameworks such as PyTorch, JAX, or TensorFlow.
* 4\+ years of professional experience working with grid modeling, simulation, state estimation, or power\-system optimization, including familiarity with physical grid constraints, utility data structures, or spatiotemporal modeling for the grid.
* A demonstrated track record of architecting systems capable of handling massive datasets or highly compute\-intensive, parallel workloads.
* Experience collaborating across technical disciplines and functions, aligning stakeholders around complex architectural decisions, and mentoring senior technical leaders.
* The ability to think from first principles and apply structured technical judgment to complex, ambiguous problems spanning machine learning, physical systems, and production infrastructure.
* Strong written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to communicate complex technical concepts clearly across multidisciplinary audiences.

**It’d be great if you also had one or more of these:**


* Experience applying machine learning to physical, interconnected networks.
* Familiarity with commercial grid\-simulation software or numerical solvers, such as PSS®E, GridLAB\-D, or MATPOWER, alongside scientific Python tools.
* A history of open\-source contributions or peer\-reviewed publications at leading AI conferences, such as NeurIPS, ICML, or ICLR, and/or power\-systems conferences associated with the IEEE Power \& Energy Society.
* Experience operating in a startup, high\-growth, or rapidly evolving technical environment.

**Tapestry Values**


* **Take charge:** We take initiative and own outcomes that move the mission forward.
* **Transform with purpose:** We build solutions that solve real problems and create meaningful impact.
* **Be a Tapestry, not a thread:** We collaborate across diverse skills and perspectives to achieve more than we can individually.
* **Always fine\-tune:** We stay curious, seek feedback, and refine our understanding as we learn.
* **Stay grounded:** We listen openly, value different perspectives, and stay focused on what matters most.

**What we offer:**


A culture that supports growth, ownership, and meaningful impact, along with…


* Competitive salary and equity
* Medical, dental, and vision coverage
* Generous PTO and flexible hybrid work model
* 401(k) with employer contribution
* Professional development
* The ability to work on important real\-world problems within an Alphabet\-backed environment

The US base salary range for this full\-time position is $262,000 \- $361,000 \+ bonus \+ equity \+ benefits. Within the range, individual pay is determined by work location and additional factors, including job\-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Your recruiter can share more about the specific salary range for your location during the hiring process.


Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include bonus, equity, or benefits.


**An Equal Opportunity Workplace**
----------------------------------


At X, we don't just accept difference \- we celebrate it, we support it, and we thrive on it for the benefit of our employees, our products and our community. We are proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. We are committed to equal employment opportunity regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, sex, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, gender identity or Veteran status. We also consider qualified applicants regardless of criminal histories, consistent with legal requirements.


If you have a disability or special need that requires accommodation, please contact us at x\-accommodation\-request@x.team.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/X-Development,,https://www.x.company,Mountain View,"1,001 to 5,000",,,,,,,,,311500.0
in-ae2da9058d610aa0,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=ae2da9058d610aa0,http://www.indeed.com/job/senior-software-engineer-ae2da9058d610aa0,Senior Software Engineer,,"Seattle, WA, US",2026-07-22,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,140000.0,160000.0,USD,False,,,,,"About ChatSlide ChatSlide (Dr. Lambda Inc.) is an AI content\-creation platform used by 240,000\+ registered creators, including professionals at major hospital systems and government agencies. We turn documents, data, and ideas into presentation decks, videos, and voiceovers in minutes. The company is headquartered in Palo Alto, CA and is expanding its U.S. engineering team, starting with this Seattle role. The Role You will be the first hire of our expansion team and own core product systems end to end, from the AI generation pipeline to the user\-facing editor, working directly with the founding team to ship features used by hundreds of thousands of creators. What You'll Do \- Design, build, and scale ChatSlide's AI content generation pipeline and backend services \- Ship user\-facing features across the Next.js frontend and Python backend \- Improve system reliability, performance, and cost efficiency across AWS and GCP infrastructure \- Integrate and evaluate state\-of\-the\-art AI models for slides, video, and voice generation \- Set engineering standards through code review, testing, and mentorship as the team grows What We're Looking For \- 5\+ years of professional software engineering experience \- Strong programming skills in Python and TypeScript/JavaScript \- Production experience with cloud infrastructure (AWS and/or GCP) \- Experience building with LLMs or other generative AI systems is a plus \- Strong product sense and ability to work autonomously in a small team Compensation \& Benefits \- $140,000 to $160,000/year plus equity options \- Flexible work arrangements \- Professional development budget

Pay: $140,000\.00 \- $160,000\.00 per year

Work Location: In person",,https://www.indeed.comNone,,,,,,,,,,,,,150000.0
in-9f99304c14a3f287,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=9f99304c14a3f287,https://redarchsolutions.applytojob.com/apply/26fekauoL7/Software-EngineerJava-Developer?source=INDE&~,Software Engineer--Java Developer,Red Arch Solutions,"Annapolis Junction, MD, US",2026-07-22,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,145000.0,211000.0,USD,False,,,,Careers@RedArchSolutions.com,"Red Arch is hiring a **Software Engineer\-Java Developer**  

to join our team!  

  

**Position Detail:**  

We are seeking an experienced Senior Java Developer to modernize a critical government information system. The ideal candidate will have deep expertise in enterprise Java application development and a proven track record of upgrading complex software infrastructures in secure, regulated environments.  

You will be responsible for planning and executing upgrades across our technology stack, including Apache Solr with Zookeeper, Apache Tomcat, Apache Directory Studio, and Java/Python components running on Windows\-based VMware infrastructure. Strong knowledge of Oracle 19c database integration, SAP Business Intelligence reporting frameworks, secure coding practices, and upgrading and migrating Solr index data is essential. Experience with PrimeFaces UI framework is a plus. You will collaborate with cross\-functional teams—including security, infrastructure, and business stakeholders—to ensure seamless upgrades with minimal operational disruption.  

Position Responsibilities:  

Core Development \& Modernization:  

* Plan and execute technology stack upgrades for enterprise Java applications in secure government environments
* Develop and maintain Java/Python components on Windows\-based VMware infrastructure
* Modernize legacy application code to current standards and best practices
* Implement secure coding practices in compliance with government security requirements


Infrastructure \& Integration:  

* Upgrade Apache Solr clusters with Zookeeper coordination
* Migrate and optimize Solr index data during version upgrades
* Manage Apache Tomcat application server configurations and deployments
* Integrate applications with Oracle 19c database systems
* Work with Apache Directory Studio for directory services integration
* Support SAP Business Intelligence reporting framework integrations


Collaboration \& Documentation:  

* Collaborate with security, infrastructure, and business stakeholder teams
* Ensure minimal operational disruption during system upgrades
* Document technical designs, upgrade procedures, and system configurations
* Participate in code reviews and knowledge\-sharing sessions

  

Education and Experience  

13\+ Years of experience in Systems or IT related roles or a highly related field of work with similar scope and responsibilities.  

A Bachelor’s degree may be substituted for 4 years of experience and a Master’s Degree may be substituted for 6 years of experience  

  

Required Quals  

* Expertise in enterprise Java application development on Windows\-based VMware infrastructure
* Expertise with Python
* Expertise Apache Solr with Zookeeper (including upgrading and migrating Solr index data)
* Experience with Apache Tomcat, Apache Directory Studio
* Experience with Oracle 19c/Relational database integration
* Experience with SAP Business Intelligence reporting frameworks
* Experience with secure coding practices for government compliance
* Ability to obtain and/or maintain a TS/SCI government clearance which requires US Citizenship

  

Desired Quals  

  

* Experience with PrimeFaces UI framework
* TS/SCI with an in\-scope polygraph

  

Work locations Annapolis Jct, MD, Washington DC, Reston VA  

Salary Range for this position $145,000 to 211,000 \#CJ ***The Red Arch Solutions pay range for this job level is a general guideline only and not a guarantee of compensation or salary. Determination of official compensation or salary relies on several factors including, but not limited to, level of position, job responsibilities, geographic location, scope of relevant work experience, educational background, certifications, contract\-specific affordability, organizational requirements, alignment with local internal equity as well as alignment with market data.***


**Red Arch Solutions Benefits Snapshot:**


* 100% paid employee healthcare premiums. CareFirst Advantage Best in Class Benefits.
* HaloScripts Concierge prescription medication service
* Generous PTO.
* 10 % 401K 6% match vested day one and up to 4% profit sharing contribution.
* Annualized bonus compensation.
* Spot bonuses for hard work.
* Tuition reimbursement.
* 529 College Saving Plan.
* College Loan Pay Back Program.
* 11 Paid Federal Holidays
* Generous Referral Bonuses.


*Red Arch Solutions provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.*


Have more questions about Red Arch? Email us at Careers@RedArchSolutions.com


