in-121db4f7b3bd03f5,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=121db4f7b3bd03f5,http://www.indeed.com/job/ai-automation-ops-associate-fixed-term-project-121db4f7b3bd03f5,AI Automation / Ops Associate - Fixed-Term Project,FleetUp,"San Jose, CA, US",2026-07-22,fulltime,direct_data,hourly,24.0,28.0,USD,False,,,,,"**About FleetUp**

FleetUp is a Global AI Fleet \& Asset Operations Platform serving enterprises, governments, insurers, and industrial operators across the US, Latin America, and the Middle East. We are moving beyond traditional telematics — building an AI\-driven operational control layer that connects vehicles, assets, cargo, drivers, and workflows into one intelligent system.

Through our **AI Convergence Project**, we are converting FleetUp's business knowledge, operational data, and customer interactions into scalable AI agents, automations, and applications — spanning AI customer support, AI dashcam video intelligence, AI reporting, and AI\-driven decision support.

**About the Role**

This is a **builder and operator role**, not a research role. And we want you to take it as a **mission, not just a job**.

Our CEO and Engineering team design and validate AI agent prototypes and automation workflows. Your mission is to take these confirmed designs and turn them into production\-grade FleetUp AI systems — then keep them running, measured, and improving.

You will work **on\-site at FleetUp HQ in San Jose**, meeting directly with the CEO of FleetUp in the office to receive designs, review builds, and shape the AI Convergence roadmap. This is a rare, front\-row opportunity to see how AI strategy is designed at the executive level and executed in production — and to grow with it.

**What You Will Do**

* **Rebuild —** Take AI agent prototypes and workflow designs confirmed by the CEO and Engineering, and re\-engineer them into stable, production\-ready builds
* **Publish —** Deploy AI agents and automations into live FleetUp operations (customer support, reporting, video labeling, internal workflows) as official FleetUp AI services
* **Operate —** Monitor performance, handle exceptions, maintain uptime, and ensure AI workflows run reliably 24/7
* **Upgrade —** Continuously improve prompts, logic, data connections, and orchestration based on performance data and new requirements
* **Document —** Maintain clear build documentation, versioning, and operational runbooks so every AI system is transferable and auditable

**Requirements**

* Hands\-on experience building with **LLM platforms and AI agents** (Claude / Anthropic API, OpenAI, or similar) — prompt design, tool use, agent workflows
* Experience with **AI orchestration and automation platforms**, especially **Make.com** (or Zapier, n8n) — multi\-step scenarios, API integrations, error handling
* Practical understanding of **AI automation and data pipelines** — connecting APIs, webhooks, CRMs (e.g., HubSpot), email, and databases into working systems
* Ability to work independently from a confirmed design: take a spec, build it, test it, ship it
* Strong written communication in English; comfortable documenting systems clearly

**Nice to Have**

* **Software engineering background** (JavaScript/Python, REST APIs, Google Apps Script) — a strong plus
* Experience operating or monitoring production automations (logging, alerting, QA)
* Familiarity with RAG, structured outputs, or AI evaluation/QA workflows
* Interest in logistics, fleet operations, IoT, or B2B SaaS

**Why This Is a Mission, Not Just a Job**

* **Real production ownership** — your builds go live to real enterprise, government, and industrial customers, not a sandbox
* **Direct access to the CEO** — regular in\-office working sessions with the CEO of FleetUp on the company's AI Convergence roadmap
* **Growth opportunity** — learn how an AI\-first company is built from the inside: strategy, build, deployment, and operations, end to end
* **Portfolio\-grade work** — ship named AI systems (support agents, video intelligence QA, automated reporting) you can point to
* **Conversion path** — strong performers will be considered for a full\-time Junior AI Engineer position at the end of the internship term

Job Type: Full\-time

Pay: $24\.00 \- $28\.00 per hour

Application Question(s):

* Will you now, or in the future, require sponsorship for employment visa status (e.g., H\-1B) to work in the United States?

