in-0ed4fb73f46fc4d5,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=0ed4fb73f46fc4d5,https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/bedrock-talent/5f459273-7dd7-47ad-8277-623684fa59f4?utm_source=D3eXzLNlpx,"Staff Engineer, Stealth Neurology Startup",,US,2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,True,,,,,"**Staff Software Engineer**
===========================

**New York City (In\-Person)**

**About Bedrock Talent**
------------------------


At Bedrock Talent, we don't try to recruit for every company.


We partner with founders we'd personally work for, teams we'd genuinely recommend to our closest friends, and companies solving problems that matter. Our clients tend to share a few things in common: they're ambitious without ego, deeply thoughtful about what they're building, and obsessed with creating products that have a real impact.


We're excited to be partnering with one of those companies today.

**About the Company**
---------------------


Our client is a confidential, seed\-stage healthcare technology startup building software that will fundamentally improve how neurological care is delivered.


While the company is still operating in stealth, they've built an exceptional founding team, have strong early momentum, and are solving a meaningful problem in one of healthcare's most underserved specialties.


Because they're still building a competitive advantage, we're keeping the search relatively selective and confidential.

**About the Opportunity**
-------------------------


This is a staff engineer role and an opportunity to join early enough that your technical decisions will shape the product, the engineering culture and long\-term direction of the company.


You'll work directly alongside the founders and a small team of exceptional engineers to build the platform from the ground up.

### **A Few Things You Should Know Up Front**


Rather than bury these details halfway through a job description, here's what usually determines whether someone gets excited about this opportunity—or realizes it isn't the right fit.

### **Five Days a Week in NYC**


This is an in\-office team.


Not because anyone wants to micromanage you, but because the founders genuinely believe that building an early\-stage company is one of the most collaborative things you can do. They enjoy working together, solving hard problems together, and believe those early years are better experienced side\-by\-side.


If you love being around smart teammates and feeding off that energy, you'll probably enjoy it here.

### **Seed Stage Means Real Ownership**


You'll receive meaningful equity and have the opportunity to influence nearly every technical decision.


It also means embracing ambiguity, moving quickly, and occasionally building without a perfect roadmap.


This role isn't for everyone—and that's okay.

### **Work That Matters**


Healthcare software doesn't have to be boring.


This team is tackling a genuinely difficult problem in neurology with the potential to improve care for both patients and providers. If you're motivated by building products that create measurable impact, you'll find plenty of purpose here.

### **You're Joining a Team, Not Starting One**


You won't be Engineer \#1\.


You'll join a small but incredibly talented engineering team that's already shipping product. You'll have the opportunity to lead technically, mentor where appropriate, and help shape what comes next.

### **Exceptional Founders**


This is probably my favorite part.


I've spent more than a decade recruiting for startups and have worked with hundreds of founders. Every so often, you meet a team that simply has what I call *good bones*.


They're thoughtful. They're humble. They're ambitious without being performative. They're building intentionally, care deeply about their people, and are exactly the type of founders I'd happily bet my own career on.


Those opportunities don't come around very often.

**What You'll Do**
------------------

* Design and build core platform capabilities using Node.js and TypeScript
* Own architectural decisions that will support long\-term scale
* Collaborate closely with founders, product, and design on product direction
* Mentor engineers through technical leadership while remaining hands\-on
* Help establish engineering best practices and shape team culture
* Ship software that directly improves the lives of healthcare providers and patients

**Tech Stack**
--------------

* TypeScript
* Node.js
* AWS
* Modern web technologies

**You Might Be a Great Fit If You...**
--------------------------------------

* Love building from zero to one.
* Enjoy solving ambiguous technical problems.
* Want meaningful ownership instead of simply maintaining existing systems.
* Care about craftsmanship as much as shipping.
* Believe the best companies are built by small teams of exceptional people working closely together.

**This Probably Isn't the Right Fit If...**
-------------------------------------------

* You're looking for a fully remote role.
* You prefer large organizations with established processes.
* You want highly defined requirements before you begin building.
* You're looking primarily for management rather than hands\-on engineering.

**Interested?**
---------------


If reading this made you think, *""That sounds like my kind of company,""* we'd love to have a conversation.


Even if the timing isn't perfect, we're always happy to connect with exceptional engineers building meaningful technology.",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,
in-51e030c34ceb5344,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=51e030c34ceb5344,https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/bedrock-talent/a3bac73b-90f0-4b0d-b2bc-90979b911225?utm_source=D3eXzLNlpx,"Senior Python Engineer, Series B Startup",,US,2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,180000.0,200000.0,USD,True,,,,,"**Senior Python Engineer**
==========================

**Remote (U.S.)**

**About Bedrock Talent**
------------------------


At Bedrock Talent, we're intentional about the companies we represent.


We don't partner with every startup that comes our way. We work with founders we'd be excited to work for ourselves, companies solving meaningful problems, and teams we genuinely believe have the potential to build category\-defining businesses.


This is one of those companies.

**About the Company**
---------------------


Our client is a fast\-growing healthcare AI startup building technology that helps healthcare providers navigate an increasingly complex reimbursement landscape.


Using machine learning, large\-scale healthcare data, and modern AI, they're creating products that transform complex payer behavior into actionable insights—helping providers reduce administrative burden, improve financial performance, and ultimately spend more time focused on patient care.


The company has assembled an exceptional technical team spanning engineering, machine learning, and data science, and is building products at the intersection of healthcare, AI, and large\-scale distributed systems.

**The Opportunity**
-------------------


We're looking for a **Senior Python Engineer** to help build the systems that power the company's next generation of AI\-driven products.


You'll work closely with engineers, machine learning researchers, and data scientists to translate sophisticated models and healthcare data into scalable, production\-ready software that customers rely on every day.


This is an ideal opportunity for someone who enjoys building backend systems, solving complex technical problems, and working on products with real\-world impact.

**Before You Apply**
--------------------


Rather than bury the important details in a long job description, here are the things that usually determine whether someone gets excited about this opportunity—or realizes it probably isn't the right fit.

### **You'll Solve Difficult Technical Problems**


This is a highly technical backend engineering role.


You'll build APIs, distributed systems, integrations, and data pipelines capable of processing massive amounts of healthcare data while maintaining reliability, performance, and scalability.

### **AI Is Core to the Product**


You'll help build production systems that leverage modern AI and machine learning—not as experiments, but as core product functionality.


You'll collaborate closely with machine learning engineers and data scientists to bring intelligent products into production.

### **Work That Matters**


Every improvement you make helps healthcare providers operate more efficiently in an increasingly complicated reimbursement environment.


The problems are technically challenging, commercially important, and have meaningful downstream impact on patient care.

### **Exceptional Team**


You'll work alongside an experienced group of engineers, data scientists, and technical leaders who care deeply about craftsmanship, collaboration, and building products that solve real customer problems.


That's why Bedrock Talent chose to partner with them.

**What You'll Do**
------------------

* Design and build scalable backend services and APIs.
* Develop integrations with healthcare and financial systems.
* Build reliable, observable data ingestion and processing pipelines.
* Partner with machine learning engineers to productionize AI\-powered features.
* Design high\-throughput, low\-latency distributed systems.
* Collaborate across engineering, product, and data science to deliver customer\-facing solutions.

**Tech Stack**
--------------

* Python, Java, or Scala
* SQL
* Spark
* Airflow
* Modern cloud infrastructure
* Machine Learning \& Generative AI

**We're Looking For Someone Who...**
------------------------------------

* Has 5\+ years of professional software engineering experience.
* Writes clean, maintainable, and well\-tested production code.
* Enjoys designing scalable backend systems.
* Thrives in collaborative, cross\-functional environments.
* Is curious, pragmatic, and enjoys solving difficult technical problems.
* Has experience with data\-intensive applications or distributed systems.

**Bonus Points**

* Experience building machine learning products in production.
* Experience with large\-scale data pipelines.
* Experience building high\-volume APIs.
* Experience working with healthcare data or regulated environments.

**This Role Is Probably a Great Fit If...**
-------------------------------------------

* You enjoy backend engineering more than frontend development.
* You like working closely with machine learning and data science teams.
* You're energized by technically challenging problems with real\-world impact.
* You want to help build AI\-powered products used by enterprise healthcare customers.

**This Role Probably Isn't the Right Fit If...**
------------------------------------------------

* You prefer highly repetitive feature work over systems design.
* You're looking for a role focused primarily on frontend engineering.
* You enjoy large, process\-heavy organizations more than fast\-moving startup environments.

**Why This Role?**
------------------


The most exciting backend engineering roles combine meaningful technical challenges with meaningful impact.


This opportunity offers both: you'll help build AI\-powered infrastructure that tackles some of healthcare's most complex operational problems while working alongside an exceptional technical team.


If reading this made you think, *""This sounds like exactly the kind of engineering problem I enjoy solving,""* we'd love to connect.


Compensation Range: $180K \- $200K",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,190000.0
