in-b324f68c8bb1e91c,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=b324f68c8bb1e91c,https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/bedrock-talent/ee120b0a-bb92-46c4-8fbc-136e5bda5d78?utm_source=D3eXzLNlpx,Staff Backend Engineer,,US,2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,180000.0,200000.0,USD,False,,,,,"**Staff Backend Engineer**
==========================

**Boston, MA (Hybrid)**

**About Bedrock Talent**
------------------------


At Bedrock Talent, we're intentional about the companies we represent.


We don't partner with every startup that comes our way. We work with founders we'd be excited to work for ourselves, companies solving meaningful problems, and teams we genuinely believe have the potential to build category\-defining businesses.


This is one of those companies.

**About the Company**
---------------------


Our client is an AI company at the forefront of conversational intelligence, building technology that helps organizations better understand human communication in real time.


Their platform combines cutting\-edge machine learning with developer\-first infrastructure to power products that detect harmful behavior, prevent fraud, and create safer digital experiences across enterprise and consumer applications.


With a growing customer base and a world\-class machine learning team, they're now investing heavily in the platform that brings those AI capabilities to developers and enterprise customers at scale.

**The Opportunity**
-------------------


We're looking for a **Staff Backend Engineer** to help build the APIs and backend systems that power the company's next generation of AI products.


This role sits at the intersection of platform engineering and machine learning. You'll partner closely with product, infrastructure, and ML teams to transform sophisticated voice intelligence models into scalable, reliable APIs used by customers around the world.


If you enjoy designing elegant backend systems, solving distributed systems challenges, and building products that enable other developers, this is an opportunity to have outsized impact.

**Before You Apply**
--------------------


Rather than bury the important details in a long job description, here are the things that usually determine whether someone gets excited about this opportunity—or realizes it probably isn't the right fit.

### **You'll Build the Platform Behind the Product**


This isn't an internal tooling role.


You'll build the APIs and backend infrastructure that enable customers to integrate cutting\-edge conversational AI into their own products and workflows.

### **AI Is at the Core**


The company has developed world\-class machine learning models for understanding human conversation.


Your role is to make those models accessible, scalable, and reliable through thoughtfully designed APIs and backend services.

### **Greenfield Meets Scale**


You'll have the opportunity to build new systems while also improving and scaling infrastructure that's already serving production customers.


If you enjoy balancing architecture, performance, and shipping quickly, you'll find plenty to dig into.

### **A Collaborative Engineering Culture**


Engineering, product, and machine learning work closely together.


Ideas are shared openly, technical discussions are encouraged, and engineers are trusted to influence both implementation and product direction.


That's one of the reasons Bedrock Talent chose to partner with this team.

**What You'll Do**
------------------

* Design, build, and maintain production APIs serving enterprise and developer customers.
* Partner with product and machine learning teams to deliver customer\-facing features.
* Improve system reliability, scalability, and performance.
* Help establish architectural patterns that support long\-term growth.
* Debug production systems and continuously improve platform stability.
* Mentor teammates and contribute to engineering best practices.

**Tech Stack**
--------------

* Python
* REST APIs
* Cloud Infrastructure
* Machine Learning Platforms
* Modern Backend Architecture

**We're Looking For Someone Who...**
------------------------------------

* Has extensive experience building backend systems in production.
