Hewlett Packard Enterprise is the global edge\-to\-cloud company advancing the way people live and work. We help companies connect, protect, analyze, and act on their data and applications wherever they live, from edge to cloud, so they can turn insights into outcomes at the speed required to thrive in today’s complex world. Our culture thrives on finding new and better ways to accelerate what’s next. We know diverse backgrounds are valued and succeed here. We have the flexibility to manage our work and personal needs. We make bold moves, together, and are a force for good. If you are looking to stretch and grow your career our culture will embrace you. Open up opportunities with HPE.


HPE Networking is about providing high\-performance, reliable, and secure networking solutions that enable seamless connectivity and digital transformation for organizations: https://www.hpe.com/us/en/about.html

***How You'll Make Your Mark:***

* Lead test strategy and execution for complex features and subsystems by analyzing design documents and technical specifications to define objectives, scope, and deliverables with minimal oversight.
* Own development, review, and continuous improvement of comprehensive test plans, protocols, and documentation; drive defect triage, root‑cause analysis, and verification of fixes.
* Design, implement, and maintain robust Python\-based test frameworks, harnesses, and automation suites used in CI/CD pipelines; ensure code is modular, reusable, and production\-ready.
* Leverage AI models and LLMs to accelerate test\-case generation, create prompt\-driven scenarios, parse and classify logs, detect anomalies, and prioritize test coverage.
* Architect and execute advanced security‑aware test scenarios validating encryption, authentication/authorization, access controls, firewall policies, threat emulation, and attack mitigation.
* Capture and analyze packet traces and system logs (Wireshark, tcpdump, enriched logs); produce clear, reproducible bug reports and actionable RCA for cross\-functional teams.
* Run and coordinate functional, performance, interoperability, regression, reliability, and security tests across physical and virtual lab environments and production\-like testbeds.
* Collaborate cross\-functionally with product, development, site reliability, and outsourced partners to define release criteria, improve test coverage, and influence secure\-by\-design practices.
* Mentor and lead junior engineers in test design, automation best practices, and security testing techniques; contribute to team processes, tooling, and metrics for continuous improvement.
* Contribute to building and operating production\-level test infrastructure, monitoring, reporting tooling, and CI/CD integrations to scale automated validation efforts.

***About You:***

* 4\-5\+ years professional experience in network quality assurance, network engineering, or security\-focused testing roles with demonstrated ownership of test programs.
* BS/MS in Computer Engineering, Computer Science, Computer Networking, Information Security, or related field.
* networking foundation with hands\-on experience in campus and data\-center deployments and production network troubleshooting.
* Proven expertise in Python for automation, building test frameworks, and producing production\-quality test code; solid understanding of data structures and software engineering practices.
* Experience applying AI/ML tools or LLMs to testing, log analytics, or automation workflows is highly valued.
* Strong practical security background: experience designing and executing threat\-informed tests, vulnerability validation, secure configuration checks, and collaborating with security teams.

***Knowledge and Skills:***

* In\-depth knowledge of networking protocols and architectures: TCP/IP, IPv4/IPv6, OSPF, BGP, EVPN/VxLAN, MPLS, VLANs, NAT, DHCP, DNS, and real\-world deployment patterns.
* 4–5\+ years using Python for test automation; deep familiarity with pytest or similar frameworks, CI/CD integration (Jenkins, GitHub Actions), and Git workflows.
* Demonstrated use of AI models/LLMs for test generation, log classification, anomaly detection, or automation enhancement.
* Advanced security testing skills: designing threat\-informed test cases, validating encryption/authentication, testing firewall behaviors (DMZ, SNAT/DNAT), conducting exploit validation, and collaborating on vulnerability remediation.
* Familiarity with network security tooling (IDS/IPS, firewalls, VPNs) and experience integrating security checks into automated test suites.
* Experience with virtualization, containers, and orchestration (VMware, Docker, Kubernetes), and network emulation/simulation platforms (GNS3, Mininet, EVE‑NG) for realistic testbeds.
* Some experience with VxLAN/EVPN deployments (Collapsed Core, DCI, Mhoming..)
* Strong experience capturing and analyzing packet traces and logs (Wireshark, tcpdump, system and application logs) and using those artifacts for RCA and automated diagnostics.
* Strong analytical mindset, troubleshooting proficiency, attention to detail, and a track record of driving automation, reliability, and security improvements in test programs.

