Qualcomm Technologies, Inc.
**Job Area:**
-------------

Engineering Group, Engineering Group \> CPU Engineering
**General Summary:**

Qualcomm's CAD Infrastructure team develops and operates mission\-critical engineering platforms used by thousands of engineers across CPU, DSP, AI, SoC, Physical Design, Verification, and Software organizations. We are seeking a Senior Full Stack Software Engineer to design, build, and scale modern web applications, automation platforms, data services, and AI\-enabled solutions that improve engineering productivity across the company.  



  

This role is ideal for an experienced engineer who enjoys working across the full technology stack—from intuitive front\-end user experiences to highly scalable backend services, cloud\-native infrastructure, data platforms, and AI\-driven workflows.  



  

You will collaborate closely with engineering teams, technical program managers, DevOps engineers, and infrastructure architects to deliver tools that are used daily by Qualcomm's engineering community.  

  

  

  

**Responsibilities**

* Design, develop, and maintain enterprise\-grade full stack applications used across engineering organizations.
* Build modern web UIs using React, TypeScript, and modern frontend frameworks.
* Develop scalable backend services and APIs using Python, Node.js, FastAPI, Express, or similar technologies.
* Design and implement RESTful and GraphQL APIs.
* Build and optimize large\-scale data platforms leveraging SQL and NoSQL databases.
* Develop automation workflows for engineering productivity, infrastructure management, analytics, and reporting.
* Partner with infrastructure teams to deploy and operate applications in Kubernetes and containerized environments.
* Build dashboards, reporting platforms, and data visualization tools.
* Integrate AI/ML and LLM technologies into internal engineering workflows where applicable.
* Drive software architecture discussions, technical design reviews, and best practices.
* Mentor junior engineers and contribute to engineering excellence across the team.
* Troubleshoot performance, scalability, reliability, and security issues in production environments.
Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to translate business and engineering requirements into technical solutions.  
* 

  

**Required Qualifications**

* Bachelor's, Master's, or PhD in Computer Science, Computer Engineering, or related field.
* 8\+ years of professional software development experience.
* Strong experience building and deploying full stack web applications.
* Expert\-level programming skills in Python.
* Strong experience with JavaScript/TypeScript and Node.js.
* Experience developing modern front\-end applications using React.
* Experience building REST APIs and microservices.
* Strong understanding of software design patterns, object\-oriented programming, and distributed systems.
* Experience with relational databases such as PostgreSQL, MySQL, or SQL Server.
* Experience with NoSQL databases such as MongoDB.
* Experience with Git\-based development workflows.
* Experience working in Linux environments.
* Strong debugging, performance tuning, and problem\-solving skills.
Excellent communication and collaboration skills.  
* 

  

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Experience supporting EDA, CAD, semiconductor design, verification, or high\-performance computing environments.
* Experience with Kubernetes, Docker, Rancher, or cloud\-native platforms.
* Experience with CI/CD pipelines and DevOps practices.
* Experience with message brokers such as RabbitMQ, Kafka, or similar technologies.
* Experience building data analytics and reporting solutions.
* Experience with Elasticsearch, Kibana, Splunk, or observability platforms.
* Experience with LSF, Slurm, or distributed job scheduling systems.
* Experience developing AI/LLM\-powered applications and integrations.
* Experience with authentication frameworks such as OAuth2, SAML, LDAP, or Active Directory.
Experience leading technical projects and mentoring engineers.  
* 

  

**Technical Skills**  

Front End


* React
* TypeScript
* JavaScript (ES6\+)
* Redux / Zustand
* HTML5
* CSS3
* Material UI / AG Grid
Modern UI/UX design principles  
* 

  

Back End


* Python
* FastAPI
* Node.js
* Express.js
* REST APIs
* GraphQL

Databases


* MongoDB
* PostgreSQL
* MySQL
* Redis

Infrastructure \& DevOps


* Kubernetes
* Docker
* Git
* CI/CD Pipelines
* Linux
* Terraform (preferred)

Data \& Analytics


* SQL
* Elasticsearch
* Kibana
* Splunk
* Data Pipelines

AI \& Emerging Technologies


* LLM Integration
* RAG Architectures
* Agentic AI Systems
Vector Databases  
* 

  

**What Success Looks Like**

* Deliver highly scalable platforms used by thousands of engineers.
* Increase engineering productivity through automation and self\-service solutions.
* Improve reliability, performance, and observability of critical infrastructure services.
* Lead architectural decisions for next\-generation CAD infrastructure platforms.
* Mentor engineers and elevate engineering standards across the organization.

**Why Qualcomm CAD Infrastructure?**

Join a team responsible for building the platforms that enable Qualcomm's world\-class semiconductor and AI products. Your work will directly impact engineering efficiency, design productivity, and innovation across multiple generations of Snapdragon and other leading technologies.


**Minimum Qualifications:**

* Bachelor's degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related field and 4\+ years of Hardware Engineering, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Systems Engineering, or related work experience.

OR
  

Master's degree in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related field and 3\+ years of Hardware Engineering, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Systems Engineering, or related work experience.
  

OR
  

PhD in Electrical Engineering, Computer Engineering, Computer Science, or related field and 2\+ years of Hardware Engineering, Software Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Systems Engineering, or related work experience.
