* Contribute to and shape technical design decisions, code reviews, and engineering standards, exercising judgment on trade\-offs rather than deferring them.
* Elevate the team by mentoring less experienced engineers, sharing context, and improving how the group builds \- while staying open to learning from architects, quality engineers, and peers.
* Collaborate across functions with product managers, architects, technical program managers, engineering managers, quality engineers, and business stakeholders.
* Improve the platform continuously \- performance tuning, application stability, supportability, and delivery practices.

  

A successful candidate would possess these skills:  

* The ability to operate independently with minimal direction and be trusted with ownership of meaningful work
* South technical judgement in ambiguous situations \- knowing when to decide, when to ask, and how to defend a trade\-off
* A quality\-first mindset and genuine attention to detail in what you ship
* The instinct to lift others up \- mentoring, unblocking, and modeling good engineering
* Clear, effective written and verbal communication with both technical and business audiences
* The composure to prioritize and deliver across multiple workstreams in a fast\-paced, dynamic environment

  

**The team**  

  

At Deloitte Tax LLP, our Global Employer Services (GES) Technology Group consultants help multinational clients develop programs, processes and digital offerings to manage a global workforce and the compliance obligations arising from global mobility, business travel and remote working. People within our technology group come from a diverse background \- they partner with our go\-to\-market teams and global clients to solve challenging problems and design experiences and products that anticipate what our Deloitte clients will want and solutions that keep them compliant with global and local regulations.  

  

**Qualifications**  

  

Required:  

* Ability to perform job responsibilities within a hybrid work model that requires US Tax professionals to co\-locate in person 2 \- 3 days per week
* Bachelor's degree in computer science, information technology, engineering, or a related field.
* 3\+ years of software development experience in workflow automation, process management, or case management solutions \- through COTS tools such as Pega, custom development such as .NET, or a combination \- including demonstrated ownership of features or modules delivered end to end with limited oversight.
* Proven ability to work independently and make sound technical decisions, and a track record of collaborating with, guiding, or mentoring other engineers.
* Limited immigration sponsorship may be available.
* Ability to travel up to 20%, on average, based on the work you do and the clients and industries/sectors you serve.
* One of the following active accreditations obtained in process, or willing/able to obtain:
* + Licensed CPA in state of practice/primary office if eligible to sit for the CPA
	+ If not CPA eligible:
	+ - Licensed Attorney
		- Enrolled Agent
		- AWS Certified Solutions Architect
		- Certified SAFE Agile Software Engineer
		- Certified SAFE DevOps Practitioner
		- Certified SAFE Architect


  

Preferred:  

* Background supporting multinational clients
* Background with global mobility technology, workforce mobility tools, or compliance reporting solutions
* Experience with cloud infrastructure platforms such as Amazon Web Services, Microsoft Azure, or Google Cloud Platform, including networking, security controls, and deployment architecture
* Experience with DevOps or DevSecOps practices, continuous integration/continuous deployment tooling, and infrastructure as code
* Experience applying cybersecurity or compliance frameworks such as National Institute of Standards and Technology, ISO 27001, SOC 2, or data privacy standards such as General Data Protection Regulation
* Experience with monitoring, logging, deployment, testing, and other application tooling platforms, as well as Jira, ServiceNow, Azure DevOps, or similar program tracking or information technology service management tools
* Pega or TOGAF certification (or willing to obtain)
* Effective written and verbal communication and strong attention to quality.

  

