Responsibilities include defining and owning software architecture for significant subsystems; leading the design and delivery of complex, cross\-team software solutions; writing high\-quality, secure, and maintainable code; and ensuring reliability, scalability, and performance across systems. The Staff Software Engineer leads technical decision\-making, performs root\-cause analysis on systemic issues, and partners closely with product, systems, hardware, and manufacturing teams to align technical solutions with business and operational needs. This role mentors senior and junior engineers, establishes and reinforces engineering best practices, contributes to technical standards, and drives continuous improvement across the software organization.

**Required Qualifications**

* Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Software Engineering, or a related technical field (or equivalent professional experience)
* 8–12 years of professional software engineering experience
* Deep proficiency in one or more programming languages such as Java, C\+\+, Python, or similar
* Strong experience in software architecture, system design, and large\-scale software integration
* Proven ability to own and evolve complex software subsystems or platforms
* Experience with relational databases, SQL, and ORM technologies
* Advanced proficiency with version control systems and collaborative development workflows
* Ability to diagnose and resolve complex, cross\-system technical issues
* Strong technical judgment, problem\-solving, and decision\-making skills
* Excellent communication skills and ability to influence across teams without formal authority

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Experience with test\-driven development (TDD), automated testing, and quality frameworks
* Familiarity with cloud platforms, DevOps practices, and CI/CD pipelines
* Experience developing software for industrial, embedded, or mission\-critical systems
* Experience mentoring senior engineers and leading technical initiatives
* Exposure to long\-lifecycle, reliability\-critical software environments",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Digital-Dynamics,,http://www.digitaldynamics.com,Scotts Valley,11 to 50,$5M to $25M (USD),,,,,,,,170000.0
in-63dfd08f9c51457f,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=63dfd08f9c51457f,https://careers-lmi.icims.com/jobs/14302/job?utm_source=indeed_integration&iis=Job%20Board&iisn=Indeed&indeed-apply-token=73a2d2b2a8d6d5c0a62696875eaebd669103652d3f0c2cd5445d3e66b1592b0f,Sr. Power Platform Developer - Clearance Required,LMI,"Remote, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,True,,,,,"Overview:

LMI is seeking an experienced and skilled Senior Power Platform Developer with demonstrated experience in business process automation to support the U.S. Army in automating human resource processes and workflows. The ideal candidate has working level experience in the Microsoft 365 Power Platform suite, to include SharePoint, Power Apps, Power BI, Power Automate, Power Virtual Agents (Co\-Pilot Studio), Microsoft Dataverse, and AI Builder. This position supports the development of technical solutions that streamline business processes, aggregate, cleanse, and visualize data, and provide user\-friendly interfaces to interact with the data.  

LMI is a new breed of digital solutions provider dedicated to accelerating government impact with innovation and speed. Investing in technology and prototypes ahead of need, LMI brings commercial\-grade platforms and mission\-ready AI to federal agencies at commercial speed.  

Leveraging our mission\-ready technology and solutions, proven expertise in federal deployment, and strategic relationships, we enhance outcomes for the government, efficiently and effectively. With a focus on agility and collaboration, LMI serves the defense, space, healthcare, and energy sectors—helping agencies navigate complexity and outpace change. Headquartered in Tysons, Virginia, LMI is committed to delivering impactful results that strengthen missions and drive lasting value.  


Responsibilities:
* Design, develop, and implement solutions using the Microsoft Power Platform suite (SharePoint, Power Apps, Power BI, Power Automate, Power Virtual Agents (Co\-Pilot Studio), Microsoft Dataverse, and AI Builder)
* Develop and maintain applications using Power Apps
* Build data pipelines from existing Army systems
* Automate workflows and business processes using Microsoft Power Automate
* Create data visualization and reporting solutions using Power BI
* Create scalable, efficient, and secure solutions to meet customer’s business objectives
* Test and Fix bugs and refactor as necessary
* Experience working in agile and works well with an agile team (Scrum Master, UI/UX Designer, Business Analyst, etc)
* Participate in working groups and process improvement teams
* Integrate Power Platform solutions with other Microsoft services and third\-party applications
* Provide technical support, documentation, and training
* Stay up to date with the latest features and updates in Power Platform


Qualifications:

Required:* Bachelor’s degree in computer science or related field
* 10\+ years development in Microsoft technologies (3\+ years Power Platform) Proficient Power Platform development experience (Share Point, Power Apps, Power Automate, and Power BI)
* Proficient at Power BI languages (Power Query, M, DAX, SQL, R)
* Proficient in integration technologies, data connectors, APIs, and protocols
* Strong communication and problem\-solving skills
* **Active Secret Clearance Required**


Desired Qualifications:* Previous experience with DoD, Army, or Human Resources Processes
* Experience with Human Centered Design
* Certification in Agile (e.g. may include PMP\-ACP, ICP, APMG, ACI, CSM, and PSM SAFe®) and understanding of the software development process


Applicants must meet eligibility requirements for a U.S. Government security clearance. Only US Citizens are eligible for a security clearance. For this position, LMI will only consider applicants with security clearances or applicants who are eligible for security clearances, due to the nature of the work.
Job Locations: US\-Remote US\-AL\-Huntsville",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Lmi,,,,,,,,,,,,,
in-da2a410d33191580,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=da2a410d33191580,https://careers-lmi.icims.com/jobs/14300/job?utm_source=indeed_integration&iis=Job%20Board&iisn=Indeed&indeed-apply-token=73a2d2b2a8d6d5c0a62696875eaebd669103652d3f0c2cd5445d3e66b1592b0f,Full-Stack Developer with Agentic AI (Clearance Required),LMI,"Tysons, VA, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,109986.0,189154.0,USD,True,,,,,"Overview:

LMI is seeking a Full\-Stack Developer with proficiency in Agentic AI to join the Chief Technology Office development team. This position requires an individual who thrives in dynamic environments, rapidly delivering results while maintaining flexibility to adapt to shifting priorities. **This position requires an active Secret security clearance.**


LMI is a new breed of digital solutions provider dedicated to accelerating government impact with innovation and speed. Investing in technology and prototypes ahead of need, LMI brings commercial\-grade platforms and mission\-ready AI to federal agencies at commercial speed.  

Leveraging our mission\-ready technology and solutions, proven expertise in federal deployment, and strategic relationships, we enhance outcomes for the government, efficiently and effectively. With a focus on agility and collaboration, LMI serves the defense, space, healthcare, and energy sectors—helping agencies navigate complexity and outpace change. Headquartered in Tysons, Virginia, LMI is committed to delivering impactful results that strengthen missions and drive lasting value.
Responsibilities:  

Providing direct support to the multiple customers, this Full\-Stack Developer will:* Leverage advanced agentic AI tools to quickly add new functionality into existing code stacks within large, complex programs.
* Make quick, high\-impact contributions to strategically critical projects across LMI’s portfolio, ensuring program success and delivering measurable results.
* Collaborate with development teams, stakeholders, and technical leads to identify pain points in existing systems and implement solutions in an agile environment.
* Transition seamlessly between programs, applying technical expertise to prioritize and address the highest\-impact initiatives.
* Analyze customer requirements and program objectives to develop innovative solutions that align with mission needs.
* Work within multidisciplinary teams to facilitate integrations, resolve technical challenges, and adhere to development timelines.
* Ensure compliance with security protocols, government standards, and industry best practices across all projects.
* Document technical solutions and improvements for knowledge transfer between teams and programs.
* Conduct rigorous testing to guarantee performance, scalability, and reliability of updated or newly developed code.


Qualifications:
**Minimum Qualifications**
==========================

* **Eligibility for a security clearance is required**: Active Secret clearance preferred.
* 3\-5 years applying dev in a production environment
* **Experience with agentic AI coding tools**: Demonstrated proficiency using tools to enhance existing code stacks at scale.
* **Proven full\-stack development experience**: Minimum of 3–5 years in developing, maintaining, and improving front\-end and back\-end systems.
* **Knowledge of programming languages**: Proficient in at least one back\-end language (Python preferred) and one front\-end framework/tool (TypeScript preferred).
* **Experience with API development**: Familiarity with developing and consuming RESTful APIs for integration across systems.
* **Familiarity with SQL and NoSQL databases**: Strong foundational skills for managing data within relational (e.g., PostgreSQL, MySQL, SQL Server) and non\-relational (e.g., MongoDB) environments.
* **Agile methodologies**: Experience working in agile environments, including the ability to work collaboratively with multidisciplinary teams.
* **Version control proficiency**: Comfortable using Git (GitLab preferred) for code development and collaboration.
* **Experience with testing, security, DevSecOps, and CI/CD processes**: Proficient in integrating with automated testing frameworks, following security protocols, and following secure, continuous integration/continuous deployment pipelines.
* **Strong communication skills**: Capable of clearly articulating technical concepts and solutions to both technical teams and non\-technical stakeholders.

**Desired Skills**
==================

* **Advanced proficiency in agentic AI tools:** Extensive experience utilizing tools to optimize coding workflows and integrate advanced AI functionality.
* **Experience with cloud environments:** Familiarity with AWS, Azure, or Google Cloud for developing and deploying cloud\-based applications.
* **Microservices architecture:** Experience in designing and implementing microservices and containerized solutions (e.g., Docker, Kubernetes).
* **UI/UX design skills:** Knowledge of modern front\-end frameworks like React, Vue.js, or Angular to enhance user interface and experience.
* **Knowledge of DevSecOps practices:** Comprehensive understanding of secure development and deployment pipelines, including infrastructure\-as\-code tools like Terraform or Ansible.
* **Data engineering:** Experience with ETL tools, data pipeline management, and real\-time analytics platforms.
* **Security certifications:** Certifications such as Security\+ or CISSP are highly desirable.
* **Experience with Agile frameworks:** Advanced knowledge of Agile or SAFe methodologies, including participation in sprint planning and ceremonies.


Target salary range: $109,986 \- $189,154  

The salary range displayed represents the typical salary range for this position and is not a guarantee of compensation. Individual salaries are determined by various factors including, but not limited to location, internal equity, business considerations, client contract requirements, and candidate qualifications, such as education, experience, skills, and security clearances.  

Applicants must meet eligibility requirements for a U.S. Government security clearance. Only US Citizens are eligible for a security clearance. For this position, LMI will only consider applicants with security clearances or applicants who are eligible for security clearances, due to the nature of the work.
