in-a09cb9388226eef3,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=a09cb9388226eef3,https://careers.hibu.com/us/en/job/HIBHIBUSP100635/Salesforce-Developer?utm_source=indeed&utm_medium=phenom-feeds,Salesforce Developer,Hibu,"Cedar Rapids, IA, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,False,,,,applicationaccomodation@hibu.com,"Job Requirements
  
  

The primary purpose of this role will be to assist with development and integration using Force.com platform. The Salesforce Developer is a key member to our Application Development team, who is seen as a technical/ domain expert on Salesforce. The individual will rely on the proven technical skills and experience to deliver cloud implementation, customization, and development services aligned with key hibu business needs.
  
  

**Primary Responsibilities:**  

Develop and maintain visualforce, AppExchanges, Force.com pages and integration to other third party solutions
  
Identify SFDC usage problems and communicate technical / communication plans to IT/business teams
  
Build client\-specific solutions on the Force.com platform using Apex and Visual Force
  
Develop integration processes using Salesforce.com’s Web Services API and third\-party integration tools
  
Develop and apply advanced Salesforce functionality to solve business problems and create customized solutions on the Force.com platform
  
Create technical requirements and specifications as needed to support full project lifecycle
  
Analyze and assess technical strategy with customers and/or teammates related to external systems, Salesforce, and data processes
  
Own the build process including continuous integration, source control and deployment operations.
  
Build integrations between Salesforce.com and external systems using custom web services.
  
Advocates and implements standards, best practices, technical design practices and unit testing
  
Stay updated with Salesforce releases and new features, evaluate and provide recommendation for implementation based on organization’s needs.
  
Collaborate with other developers and administrators to improve overall Salesforce platform performance, scalability and security.
  
Experience with and desire to use AI\-assisted development tools. Experience with Devin or other tools is a plus.
  
  

**Critical Skills:**  

Proficiency in Apex, Visualforce, Web Services, SOQL, AJAX, XML, Javascript and Lightning web component
  
Understanding of data structure and its correlation to Salesforce: Sales \& Service Cloud, Data Loader, Custom Applications
  
Ability to work independently or in a team environment both offshore and onsite at various times with minimum direct supervision
  
Well\-versed in cloud computing technologies and concepts
  
Development experience in Agile environment
  
S trong understanding of object\-oriented programming concepts and design patterns.
  
Desire to embrace AI\-assisted development and AI solutions
  
Excellent problem\-solving and troubleshooting skills, with the ability to analyze complex business requirments and propose effective technical solutions.
  
  

**Experience:**  

Bachelor's Degree in Information Sciences, Computer Science or relevant discipline
  
3\-5 years of experience developing custom applications, preferably within Salesforce.com
  
3\-5 years of experience developing custom data integrations between multiple systems or databases
  
Strong knowledge in the following \- Eclipse/Visual Studio Code, source control, Apex, JavaScript, Lightning framework, data hygiene and security and test\-driven development
  
High proficiency in Apex, Visualforce, Force.com API, Web Services
  
Salesforce Developer Certifications not required but a plus
  
  

﻿ Working with us means joining a team of truly extraordinary people working to improve communities across the country. Joining our team means not only working in a fun environment with smart people, but also being able to take advantage of our competitive compensation, ongoing training, incentives, and generous benefits package.
  
**Learn more about the Hibu culture here:** Culture at Hibu
  
﻿
  
**NOTE:** Hibu is an Equal Opportunity Employer, and consistent with applicable law, provides reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities and disabled veterans in completing our job application process. If you need reasonable accommodation and/or are having difficulty completing our online application process due to a disability you may use the following email address applicationaccomodation@hibu.com : Please include your name and contact information and the title of the position you are interested in. Note: this is not for general employment inquires or correspondence. Hibu will only respond to requests related to those who need assistance with the online application process due to a disability
  
  

