in-717ca6b0fabc2148,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=717ca6b0fabc2148,https://jobs.lever.co/nomihealth/24a9f84e-ebc2-4c41-b8fc-14822f0dc973?lever-source=Indeed,Staff Software Engineer,Nomi Health,"Salt Lake City, UT, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,False,,,,,"We were tired of hearing that healthcare is broken, so we decided to do something about it. At Nomi Health, we believe the care itself isn’t broken — it’s the business of healthcare that gets in the way. Every year, more than $1 trillion is wasted on paperwork, delays, and middle layers that drive up costs and keep people from the care they need.

We’re rebuilding the system so it works the way it should: clear prices you can trust, faster payments that keep providers focused on patients, and data that helps employers make better decisions. Our work has already touched more than 30 million lives — from local communities in Michigan to some of the largest companies in the country.**About the Role**
------------------



Nomi Health is hiring a Staff Software Engineer to provide technical leadership for the applications and platforms powering our healthcare and financial operations.



You will lead the design and delivery of highly available systems supporting claims, remittance, payment processing, provider operations, and other critical healthcare workflows. You will work closely with engineering, product, operations, and business leaders to turn complex requirements into reliable, scalable solutions.



This is a senior individual\-contributor role for an engineer who can establish technical direction, solve ambiguous problems, raise engineering standards, and help distributed teams deliver successfully.


**What You’ll Do**
------------------


* Establish the technical direction and architecture for complex applications and platform capabilities.
* Partner with product managers and business stakeholders to evaluate implementation options, clarify tradeoffs, and define practical delivery plans.
* Lead projects through the complete software development lifecycle, from discovery and system design through implementation, testing, deployment, and production support.
* Design and build highly available healthcare and payment applications using Go, TypeScript, React, and AWS services.
* Break large, ambiguous initiatives into well\-defined technical workstreams that distributed engineering teams can execute.
* Identify architectural risks, dependencies, failure modes, and operational requirements before implementation begins.
* Review system designs and code to ensure solutions are reliable, secure, maintainable, testable, and cost\-effective.
* Establish and reinforce engineering practices related to automated testing, observability, idempotency, performance, security, and fault tolerance.
* Diagnose complex production issues and lead technical efforts to restore service and prevent recurrence.
* Mentor engineers and help them develop stronger skills in system design, problem\-solving, and technical decision\-making.
* Identify reusable components, patterns, and platform capabilities that improve delivery across teams.
* Stay current with emerging technologies and help the organization adopt tools and practices that create meaningful engineering leverage.

**What We’re Looking For**
--------------------------


### **Minimum Qualifications**


* 8\+ years of professional software development experience.
* 5\+ years of experience testing, launching, and supporting production software.
* 3\+ years of experience designing software systems and defining application or platform architecture.
* Experience leading technically complex projects involving multiple engineers or teams.
* Strong understanding of distributed systems, APIs, data modeling, automated testing, and production operations.
* Experience developing cloud\-based applications in a high\-availability or high\-throughput environment.
* Ability to communicate technical decisions, risks, and tradeoffs clearly to both technical and nontechnical stakeholders.

### **Preferred Qualifications**


* Experience building production services with Go.
* Experience with AWS services such as Lambda, API Gateway, S3, CloudFront, EventBridge, Step Functions, and Secrets Manager.
* Experience with serverless and event\-driven architectures.
* Experience with TypeScript, React, GraphQL, Temporal, MongoDB, Snowflake, or Bazel.
* Experience in healthcare, fintech, payments, claims processing, or other regulated industries.
* Familiarity with payment rails such as ACH, wires, checks, or virtual cards.
* Experience leading architecture reviews or setting technical standards across multiple teams.
* Experience using AI\-assisted or agentic development tools to improve software delivery.

**What Success Looks Like**
---------------------------



A successful Staff Software Engineer at Nomi Health does more than deliver individual features. You establish technical clarity, help teams make better decisions, reduce operational risk, and leave behind systems and engineering practices that make future work easier.



Nomi Health delivers disruptive healthcare solutions, in partnership with like\-minded employers, public sector organizations, advisors (brokers/consultants), and payers/TPAs. We’re a team of 300\+ people who show up every day with the same mindset: don’t settle for “that’s just how it is.” Real change happens when you challenge the system, cut through the excuses, and build something better together.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Nomi-Health,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/0fd6c69de07ce5ed3381c404dc751c86,http://nomihealth.com,"Orem, UT",201 to 500,Decline to state,"Nomi’s journey is just starting in delivering disruptive healthcare solutions, in partnership with like-minded employers, public sector organizations, advisors (brokers/consultants), and payers/TPAs. ",,,,,,,
in-310c67ed1734e34a,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=310c67ed1734e34a,https://alkami.wd12.myworkdayjobs.com/en-US/alkami/job/US-Remote/Sr-Software-Engineer_JR-000767,Sr Software Engineer,Alkami Technology,"Remote, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,130000.0,165000.0,USD,True,,,,,"Alkami is the digital sales and service platform provider for U.S. banks and credit unions. Our unified Platform integrates onboarding, digital banking, and data and marketing—each solution can stand alone, but together they deliver more—to help institutions onboard, engage, and grow relationships. As the future shifts toward Anticipatory Banking, we help data\-informed bankers meet the moment with technology that drives action.

  

Founded in 2009, we continue to be recognized for our intentional culture and tremendous growth (Best Place to Work in Fintech; Best \& Brightest to Work For Nationally; and Comparably’s Best Company Culture, Best Career Growth, Best Engineering Team, and Best Places to Work in Dallas, among others). We’re building a culture where each Alkamist can perform to their highest potential, and we’re always on the lookout for the best and brightest minds. If you’re ready to experience the power of alchemy \- transforming the ordinary into the extraordinary \- come join one of the fastest growing SaaS companies in the U.S.

  

As a remote\-first company, most of our positions can be remote in the US, except for key roles, which will be indicated in the Job Title.

  

Follow us on Glassdoor and LinkedIn!


The Senior Software Engineer will drive efforts and contribute to building software systems on Alkami's Account Experience team — the core UI layer powering Alkami's Online Banking (OLB) platform. This is an emerging team with a front\-end\-leaning charter: owning the My Accounts widget, landing page experiences, and micro\-experiences that drive direct user engagement across Alkami's multi\-tenant environment. We're looking for demonstrated, deep technical domain knowledge including apps, services, systems, or frameworks. A key strategic player involved in maintenance of product features, including on\-call escalations, triaging, and resolution.
**Essential Duties \&** **Responsibilities**

* Lead code/design reviews to ensure smooth daily operations and accurate planning
* Participate in the entire application lifecycle, with a focus on front\-end coding, debugging, and UI performance
* Write clean, reusable code for functional, high\-quality web applications within a multi\-tenant SaaS environment
* Advanced troubleshooting and debugging across FE and service\-level code
* Perform UI tests to optimize performance and user experience
* Liaise with developers, designers, and system administrators to identify and deliver new front\-end features
* Manage cutting\-edge technologies to improve and modernize legacy applications (e.g. migration from Knockout to Vue.js)
* Build reusable component libraries and front\-end frameworks for future use
* Provide mentoring and technical support to junior engineers
* Respond promptly to on\-call incidents, including troubleshooting and resolving critical disruptions
* Maintain clear and proactive communication with customers and vendors
* Champion an API\-first approach, ensuring seamless integration, scalability, and extensibility
* Applies AI\-assisted workflows to enhance productivity in code generation, testing, and refactoring

**Recommended Experience \& Education**

***Minimum Years of Experience***


Typically requires a minimum of 5 years of related experience; or 3 years and an advanced degree


Education Level Bachelor’s degree in engineering, or another related field or equivalent work experience

**Knowledge, Skills, \& Qualifications**

**Required**

* 5\+ years of software development experience; or 3 years with an advanced degree
* True full\-stack capability with a front\-end preference — approximately 75% FE / 25% BE service\-level work
* Strong proficiency in Vue.js (primary); React or Angular also acceptable \- should genuinely be comfortable with front\-end work
* Proficiency in C\#/.NET for service\-level backend code
* Experience with SQL Server and/or PostgreSQL
* In\-depth understanding of the full software development lifecycle (design, development, deployment)
* Experience developing and deploying applications on cloud\-native infrastructure
* Strong experience with REST API best practices — security, scalability, performance
* Experience in SQL and NoSQL databases, caching strategies, and data structure design
* Proficiency with observability tooling (Prometheus, Grafana or equivalent)
* Demonstrated ability to leverage modern AI tooling in day\-to\-day engineering workflows
* Excellent analytical, communication, and time management skills
* Proven ability to work cross\-functionally with engineering and product teams
* Ability to participate in on\-call rotation to support Alkami's customers

**Preferred**

* Experience in fintech or banking (deposits, CD accounts, treasury management, or similar financial domain knowledge strongly preferred)
* Experience with SaaS offerings in the technology and financial services industries
* Experience building and deploying on AWS using Kubernetes
* Experience with OpenTelemetry
* Experience with cross\-platform mobile frameworks such as Flutter


The salary range for this position is: $130,000 \- $165,000**Cool Things to Know**
=======================

**Not Just Any Company**: Alkami has an awesome diverse and inclusive environment. We have a FUN culture and offer great benefits, including remote\-first environment, unlimited paid time off, 401(k) with employer match, and more.

**Work Authorization**: We cannot offer employment sponsorship at this time. Candidates must be eligible to work in the US for full\-time employment.

**Recruiters**: We are not looking for outside recruiting firms to help us in this search. Thank you for understanding.

**Pay Transparency:** As of January 1, 2023, new states and locales have enacted pay equity laws that require more pay transparency by employers in the following states: California, Colorado (effective January 1, 2021\), Connecticut, Maryland, Nevada, New Jersey, New York, Ohio, Rhode Island and Washington.


**The Important Stuff**
=======================

