-----------------------

**What you'll do...**
---------------------


As a Software Engineer III at Walmart, you will lead the design and development of scalable software solutions by collaborating with cross\-functional teams including product management and user experience. You will troubleshoot complex issues, perform root cause analysis, and implement sustainable solutions while ensuring high\-quality code and adherence to security standards. This role involves managing projects of varying complexity, supporting continuous integration and delivery, and mentoring junior engineers. Your technical expertise and problem\-solving skills will contribute to delivering impactful technology that supports Walmart’s business objectives and operational excellence.

 **About the team:**  

The Subscriptions Team supports one of the largest e\-commerce platforms globally, managing critical systems that process billions of transactions annually with high reliability and speed. The team delivers scalable, innovative solutions enhancing the shopping experience from selection to checkout, integrating AI\-driven recommendations and omnichannel features. Collaborating with experienced engineers, team members engage in continuous learning and technical growth within a dynamic environment. Their work directly advances Walmart’s business goals and customer satisfaction by ensuring seamless, efficient commerce experiences through robust platform design and development.  

**What you'll do:**

* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams to define high\-level design and technical solutions for projects.
* Develop, test, and maintain scalable, secure, and high\-quality software components and applications.
* Troubleshoot and resolve production issues through root cause analysis and effective action plans.
* Lead small engineering groups by providing guidance, documentation, and mentorship.
* Implement automation scripts to support continuous integration and delivery processes.
* Ensure adherence to coding standards, security policies, and quality requirements.
* Monitor application performance and participate in defect management and regression testing.
* Support business needs by evaluating technical feasibility and recommending solutions.

**What you'll bring:**

* 4\+ years of experience in software development, with 3\+ years in Android development Kotlin
* Experience developing and testing Serverside APIs for mobile and web clients using Node.js, Java, Go, etc. GraphQL APIs using Apollo is a plus.
* Work with Kotlin, Coroutines, Flow/LiveData, MVVM \& MVI architectures, Retrofit, GraphQL
* Experience with Android framework components and their lifecycles; strong knowledge of multithreading, networking performance tuning.
* Experience with Android SDKs, Jetpack libraries, and lifecycle\-aware architecture.
* Familiarity with public cloud technologies such as Azure
* Demonstrated ability to manage complex projects, translating requirements into scalable, maintainable solutions.
* Familiarity with cloud platforms such as Microsoft Azure.

**About Walmart Global Tech**  

Imagine working in an environment where one line of code can make life easier for hundreds of millions of people. That’s what we do at Walmart Global Tech. We’re a team of software engineers, data scientists, cybersecurity expert's and service professionals within the world’s leading retailer who make an epic impact and are at the forefront of the next retail disruption. People are why we innovate, and people power our innovations. We are people\-led and tech\-empowered. We train our team in the skillsets of the future and bring in experts like you to help us grow. We have roles for those chasing their first opportunity as well as those looking for the opportunity that will define their career. Here, you can kickstart a great career in tech, gain new skills and experience for virtually every industry, or leverage your expertise to innovate at scale, impact millions and reimagine the future of retail.


Walmart’s culture is a competitive advantage, and it’s fostered by being together. Working together in person allows us to collaborate, align quickly and innovate with greater speed. We use our campuses to create purposeful connection rooted in deepening understanding and investing in the development of our associates.  

Our hubs: Walmart is a global company with offices across the United States and around the world. Our global headquarters is in Bentonville, Arkansas, with primary hubs in the San Francisco Bay area and New York/New Jersey.

 **Benefits:**  

Benefits: Beyond our great compensation package, you can receive incentive awards for your performance. Other great perks include 401(k) match, stock purchase plan, paid maternity and parental leave, PTO, multiple health plans, and much more.  

  

**Equal Opportunity Employer:**  

Walmart, Inc. is an Equal Opportunity Employer – By Choice. We believe we are best equipped to help our associates, customers, and the communities we serve live better when we really know them. That means understanding, respecting, and valuing unique styles, experiences, identities, ideas, and opinions – while being inclusive of all people.  

  

