in-0fe24e566efdb3ba,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=0fe24e566efdb3ba,https://discordapp.com/jobs/8642085002,"Senior Full-Stack Software Engineer, Growth",Discord,"San Francisco Bay Area, CA, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,196000.0,220000.0,USD,False,,,,,"Discord has a highly engaged community of millions of daily active users who use the platform for many different reasons, but there’s one thing that nearly everyone does: play video games. Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming, and we are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to hang out before, during, and after playing games.Discord has a highly engaged community of millions of daily active users who use the platform for many different reasons, but there's one thing that nearly everyone does: play video games. Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming, and we are focused on making it easier and more fun for people to hang out before, during, and after playing games. We're looking for a Senior Software Engineer to join the Growth team at Discord. Our team owns how new users discover, understand, and get started with Discord — from the first moment someone encounters us on the web through the onboarding experience that turns them into engaged members. You'll work across the stack to build the systems that acquire and activate users at scale, whether that means improving how Discord shows up across the web or designing the in\-product experiences that help new users find their footing. This is a high\-impact role where you'll directly influence how Discord grows. This person will report to the Senior Engineering Manager for Growth. What you'll be doing: Build and optimize user\-facing experiences that improve how people discover, understand, and get started with Discord Develop scalable backend systems that serve dynamic, high\-performance content at scale Work across the full stack — frontend (TypeScript, React) and backend (Python) — wherever the problem leads Design and run A/B experiments to measure the impact of your work on user acquisition and activation Partner with Product, Design, and Data Science to identify high\-impact growth opportunities and iterate quickly Maintain performance and reliability standards for user\-facing properties Write code that's readable, reviewable, and built with the next engineer in mind What you should have: 3\+ years of professional software engineering experience shipping production web products Strong expertise in TypeScript and React with a track record of delivering high\-performance frontend experiences Practical experience with Python and backend frameworks such as Flask Experience designing and running A/B tests with a focus on data\-driven decision making Comfort working across the full stack and taking ownership of projects end to end A habit of asking why before asking how — and the judgment to know when good enough ships and when it doesn't Bonus points: Prior experience on growth\-focused engineering teams working on activation, onboarding, or acquisition Experience building SEO infrastructure, or interest in how LLMs and search engines index and surface web content Mobile development experience The US base salary range for this full\-time position is $196,000 to $220,000\+ equity \+ benefits. Our salary ranges are determined by role and level. Within the range, individual pay is determined by additional factors, including job\-related skills, experience, and relevant education or training. Please note that the compensation details listed in US role postings reflect the base salary only, and do not include equity, or benefits.Why Discord?Discord plays a uniquely important role in the future of gaming. We're a multiplatform, multigenerational and multiplayer platform that helps people deepen their friendships around games and shared interests, and helps developers build and grow their businesses. We believe games give us a way to have fun with our favorite people, whether listening to music together or grinding in competitive matches for diamond rank. Join us in our mission! Your future is just a click away! Discord is committed to inclusion and providing reasonable accommodations during the interview process. We want you to feel set up for success, so if you are in need of reasonable accommodations, please let your recruiter know. Please see our Applicant and Candidate Privacy Policy for details regarding Discord’s collection and usage of personal information relating to the application and recruitment process by clickingHERE.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Discord,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/69c3e6df6e321e61d3b408ca9250e884,https://www.discord.com,San Francisco,"501 to 1,000",$25M to $100M (USD),"Discord is a voice, video and text app that helps friends and communities come together to hang out and explore their interests.",,,,,,,208000.0
in-da4b047b6a4b5823,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=da4b047b6a4b5823,https://phg.tbe.taleo.net/phg02/ats/careers/v2/viewRequisition?org=NUAXINNO&cws=39&rid=4083,Appian Developer Mid,NuAxis Innovations,"Washington, DC, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,False,,,,,"**We are a federal IT company on a mission to make customer experience (CX) the center of every government solution.**

**Technology is our Passion. People are our Purpose.**


We know tech, but we love people. NuAxis is home to thinkers and feelers; engineers and artists. We work hard and support each other along the way. Teamwork is more than just a buzzword for us, it’s a state of mind.


We believe happy employees do amazing work, so join our team NOW! We are currently seeking a talented and motivated **Appian Developer Mid** for a Full\-Time position.

**Position Summary**
--------------------


We are seeking a **Mid Level Appian Integration Developer** to support the continued development, enhancement, and maintenance of Case Management System on Appian platform. This role primarily focuses on Appian application development while also supporting enterprise integrations through the DataHub. The ideal candidate will spend approximately half of their time developing Appian applications and workflows and the remaining time building, maintaining, and supporting integrations between Appian and Kafka based event streaming services.


This role is ideal for an Appian developer who enjoys working with APIs, Java based integrations, cloud technologies, and event driven architectures. The developer will work closely with business analysts, architects, infrastructure engineers, and partner agencies to deliver secure, scalable, and reliable solutions supporting the federal customer.

**Responsibilities**

* The developer will design, develop, test, deploy, and maintain Appian applications, including process models, interfaces, records, reports, integrations, and business rules supporting the FLAG case management system. The role includes troubleshooting production issues, optimizing application performance, implementing new business capabilities, participating in Agile development activities, and maintaining technical documentation.
* The developer will also support the DataHub by developing and maintaining integrations between Appian, REST APIs, and Kafka based event streaming services. Responsibilities include consuming and publishing Kafka events, troubleshooting integration issues, supporting schema validation, monitoring event processing, and assisting with the migration to AWS Managed Streaming for Kafka (MSK). The role includes working with cloud infrastructure, Oracle databases, and enterprise APIs to ensure reliable and secure data exchange between FLAG and external partner systems.
* The developer will collaborate with technical teams to onboard new partner agencies, implement API integrations, support identity federation and secure authentication, maintain system documentation, participate in code reviews, contribute to continuous improvement initiatives, and support security, compliance, and Authority to Operate (ATO) activities.

**Required Qualifications**

* Candidates should have a bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, or a related field, or equivalent experience, along with four or more years of professional software development experience.
* Candidates should have at least three years of Appian development experience, including process models, interfaces, records, expression rules, integrations, web APIs, and application deployment. Experience building enterprise workflows and integrating Appian with external systems is required.
* Candidates should also have experience with Java, REST APIs, JSON, SQL, and relational databases, preferably Oracle. Experience working with Apache Kafka or similar messaging technologies is highly desirable, including publishing and consuming events through APIs or messaging services. Experience with AWS cloud services, Git, CI/CD pipelines, Agile development, and API security using OAuth or JWT is preferred.


Candidates must be eligible to obtain and maintain a Department of Labor Public Trust clearance.

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Preference will be given to candidates with Appian Associate Developer or Senior Developer certification, experience supporting Federal Government systems, and familiarity with Kafka, AWS Managed Streaming for Kafka (MSK), REST APIs, Oracle, and cloud based integrations. Experience with Appian plug ins, Java development, Section 508 compliance, and enterprise case management systems is highly desirable.

**Does this opportunity sound like a fit for you? If so, join our talent community and click to apply now!!**

**Our Profile:**


We are an IT company with a unique mission—to make people the center of every federal IT solution. Our technologists have always gone the extra mile to help our federal clients succeed. And over the years, we saw a growing disconnect in how federal IT initiatives were built and managed. Time after time, programs failed because the focus was on the tools and products and not the people using them. **Learn More****.**


NuAxis is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment is contingent upon successful completion of a background investigation. **Learn More** about our Benefits and Culture!",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Nuaxis-Innovations,,,,,,,,,,,,,
