NTT DATA strives to hire exceptional, innovative and passionate individuals who want to grow with us. If you want to be part of an inclusive, adaptable, and forward\-thinking organization, apply now.
  
  

We are currently seeking a Oracle Cloud HCM Reporting Analytics Developer \- Hybrid/Onsite to join our team in Fort Worth, Texas (US\-TX), United States (US).
  
  

Oracle Cloud HCM Reporting Analytics Developer
  
  

Position Summary
  
  

We are seeking an experienced Oracle Cloud HCM Reporting Analytics Developer to design, develop, and support enterprise HR reporting and analytics solutions. In this role, you will leverage Oracle Fusion Data Intelligence (FDI), Oracle Transactional Business Intelligence (OTBI), and advanced SQL to deliver dashboards, reports, and data insights that support HR operations and strategic decision\-making.
  
  

The ideal candidate has strong Oracle Cloud HCM reporting expertise, a solid understanding of HR data and business processes, and experience transforming complex data into meaningful analytics for HR and business leaders.
  
  

Key Responsibilities
  
  

Oracle Cloud HCM Reporting
  
* Design, develop, and maintain HR reports, dashboards, scorecards, and analytics using Oracle Fusion Data Intelligence (FDI) and Oracle Transactional Business Intelligence (OTBI).
* Develop recurring, scheduled, and ad hoc reports that support HR operations and executive decision\-making.
* Build reporting solutions using Oracle Cloud HCM data, including subject areas, datasets, and reporting models.
* Develop and maintain HCM Extracts and Oracle BI Publisher (BIP) reports where required.
* Manage reporting security, access profiles, and role\-based permissions to ensure appropriate access to confidential HR data.


Data Analytics SQL Development
  
* Write and optimize complex SQL queries to extract, transform, validate, and analyze HR data.
* Design scalable datasets and data models that support dashboards and operational reporting.
* Source, integrate, and transform data from Oracle Cloud HCM and related systems.
* Perform data validation, reconciliation, and troubleshooting to ensure reporting accuracy and integrity.


Dashboard Business Intelligence Development
  
* Build interactive dashboards, visualizations, trend analysis, KPIs, and executive reporting.
* Deliver user\-friendly reporting solutions that provide actionable workforce insights.
* Automate recurring reporting processes and improve reporting efficiency.


Data Quality Reporting Governance
  
* Develop automated validation and quality control processes for HR reporting.
* Identify data issues and partner with HRIS and IT teams to improve data quality and reporting reliability.
* Support testing for Oracle Cloud releases, reporting enhancements, and system integrations.


Stakeholder Collaboration
  
* Partner with HR, HRIS, IT, and business leaders to gather reporting requirements and deliver scalable reporting solutions.
* Translate business requirements into meaningful analytics and reporting deliverables.
* Document reporting logic, data definitions, and technical specifications to support ongoing maintenance and knowledge transfer.


Required Qualifications
  
* Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, Information Systems, HRIS, Business, or a related field (or equivalent experience).
* 5\+ years of experience developing HR reporting and analytics solutions.
* 5\+ years of hands\-on experience with Oracle Fusion Data Intelligence (FDI).
* 5\+ years of experience developing reports and dashboards using Oracle Transactional Business Intelligence (OTBI).
* Advanced SQL development skills, including complex queries, joins, subqueries, and data transformation.
* Experience developing dashboards, operational reports, scheduled reports, and analytics solutions.
* Strong understanding of relational databases, data modeling, and data warehouse concepts.
* Experience validating, reconciling, and troubleshooting HR data.
* Strong knowledge of Oracle Cloud HCM data structures, subject areas, and reporting architecture.
* Ability to communicate effectively with both technical and non\-technical stakeholders.


Preferred Qualifications
  
* Experience with Oracle Cloud HCM Extracts.
* Experience with Oracle BI Publisher (BIP).
* Experience with Tableau, Power BI, SQL Developer, or other enterprise BI tools.
* Experience with ETL processes, data integration, or enterprise data warehouses.
* Experience supporting Oracle Cloud quarterly releases, UAT, and production deployments.
* Experience working within HRIS, People Analytics, or Workforce Analytics teams.
* Knowledge of HR business processes, employee lifecycle reporting, and HR data governance.


**Travel:** None
  
  

**Education:** Bachelor's degree in a related field or equivalent professional experience.
  
  

Pay Transparency
  
  

Where required by law, NTT DATA provides a reasonable range of compensation for specific roles. The starting pay range for this remote role is $92,408\-$171,125\. This range reflects the minimum and maximum target compensation for the position across all US locations. Actual compensation will depend on a number of factors, including the candidate’s actual work location, relevant experience, technical skills, and other qualifications.
  
  

This position is eligible for company benefits including medical, dental, and vision insurance with an employer contribution, flexible spending or health savings account, life and ADD insurance, short\- and long\-term disability coverage, paid time off, employee assistance, participation in a 401k program with company match, and additional voluntary or legally\-required benefits.
  
  

About NTT DATA
  
  

NTT DATA is a $30\+ billion business and technology services leader, serving 75% of the Fortune Global 100\. We are committed to accelerating client success and positively impacting society through responsible innovation. We are one of the world’s leading AI and digital infrastructure providers, with unmatched capabilities in enterprise\-scale AI, cloud, security, connectivity, data centers and application services. Our consulting and industry solutions help organizations and society move confidently and sustainably into the digital future. As a Global Top Employer, we have experts in more than 50 countries. We also offer clients access to a robust ecosystem of innovation centers as well as established and start\-up partners. NTT DATA is part of NTT Group, which invests over $3 billion each year in RD.
  
  

Whenever possible, we hire locally to NTT DATA offices or client sites. This ensures we can provide timely and effective support tailored to each client’s needs. While many positions offer remote or hybrid work options, these arrangements are subject to change based on client requirements. For employees near an NTT DATA office or client site, in\-office attendance may be required for meetings or events, depending on business needs. At NTT DATA, we are committed to staying flexible and meeting the evolving needs of both our clients and employees. NTT DATA recruiters will never ask for payment or banking information and will only use @nttdata.com and @talent.nttdataservices.com email addresses. If you are requested to provide payment or disclose banking information, please submit a contact us form, https://us.nttdata.com/en/contact\-us.
  
  

