Direct reports: None. Delta's provide performance feedback on other engineers and participate in company peer mentorship program.



Travel: 0\-10%

  



The Role



As a Mid\-Level Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE), you will contribute directly to the development and delivery of Palantir capabilities. You will build analytical dashboard features, support CI/CD pipeline tasks, and work within a structured agile environment alongside senior engineers and government stakeholders. You will operate in two\-week sprint cycles, contributing to feature delivery from design through deployment.



At our organization, an FDE takes ownership of their work — building reliable features, writing meaningful code, and ensuring each sprint increment is production\-ready.

  



Key Responsibilities


* Provide embedded engineering support for the Palantir system, working alongside operational users and senior engineers to deliver mission\-aligned capabilities
* Perform data integration and ontology engineering tasks, including building and maintaining pipelines, implementing metric definitions, and aligning data transformations to the Foundry Ontology to ensure consistent interpretation across the platform
* Develop workflows, applications, dashboards, and AI\-enabled features using Foundry's Workshop/Slate application layer under guidance from senior engineers
* Participate in intake, triage, and solution framing activities — helping translate user needs and stakeholder requests into well\-scoped engineering work
* Contribute to production hardening and transition efforts, including CI/CD pipeline configuration, build scripts, automated tests, and environment promotion workflows to ensure features are deployment\-ready
* Support sustainment and iterative improvement operations by resolving defects, delivering incremental enhancements, and maintaining stable operations across deployed capabilities
* Produce clear technical documentation, including configuration notes, runbooks, and sprint artifacts
* Participate in sprint planning, daily standups, sprint reviews, and demonstrations for government stakeholders
* Conduct testing and validation to confirm workflows, dashboards, and AI features function correctly and that data aligns with approved definitions
* Identify integration issues, surface blockers early, and collaborate with senior engineers to resolve them

  



Preferred Qualifications


* Hands\-on experience with Palantir Foundry, including pipelines, Workshop/Slate, and Ontology
* 3\+ years of software engineering experience
* Experience with Python, TypeScript, or Java in cloud\-based data platforms
* Experience working in government, defense, or classified environments
* Ability to independently build features, test them, and deliver production\-ready functionality
* Comfortable working in small, fast\-moving technical teams

  



About PVM \& Benefits



At PVM, we mean it when we say we value diversity. As a PVM team member, you will work with people from all different backgrounds that are passionate about the problems we solve for our customers and are focused on delivering value for our clients. Our culture encourages problem solving, leadership, and innovation, and creates an environment that will support your professional and personal growth. Here are a few highlights of the advantages of being a part of the PVM community:


* Opportunities for growth and advancement
* Tuition/Training reimbursement
* Peer bonus program
* Remote and on\-site positions available
* Unlimited PTO
* Flexible work schedule

  



PVM delivers digital services that help government agencies unlock the power of their data for good and maximize the value of their technology investments. We design, develop, and deploy solutions to solve mission\-critical problems. PVM is a black\- and service\-disabled veteran\-owned small business and was founded by a retired Naval officer out of frustration with the status quo with one goal in mind: to help his fellow Shipmates solve the problems they were facing every day. Today, we continue to be driven by that same goal and are focused on taking on our clients' missions as our own to make a difference in the communities we serve. PVM believes in equal opportunity employment. We won't discriminate against any employee or applicant based on race, gender, nationality, age, religion, disability, military status, or sexual orientation. As a company and as individuals, we're committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for our team, our family members, and our clients.",,"https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Pvm,-Inc.",,,,,,,,,,,,,
in-cadc78f41f3dc32b,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=cadc78f41f3dc32b,https://grnh.se/b5hfioar5us,Senior Mobile Engineer,AssetWatch,US,2026-07-21,,direct_data,yearly,165000.0,190000.0,USD,True,,,,,"AssetWatch serves global manufacturers by powering manufacturing uptime through the delivery of an unparalleled condition monitoring experience, with a passion to care about the assets our customers care for every day. We are a devoted and capable team that includes world\-renowned engineers and distinguished business leaders united by a common goal – To build the future of predictive maintenance. As we enter the next phase of rapid growth, we are seeking people to help lead the journey.



AssetWatch serves global manufacturers by powering manufacturing uptime through the delivery of an unparalleled condition monitoring experience, with a passion to care about the assets our customers care for every day. We are a devoted and capable team that includes world\-renowned engineers and distinguished business leaders, united by a common goal: to build the future of predictive maintenance. As we enter the next phase of rapid growth, we are seeking people to help lead the journey.



As a Senior Mobile Engineer, you will be a senior, hands\-on contributor on our mobile team, building and shaping our Flutter applications while staying fluent across the services that power them. The mobile experience supports field technicians, customer teams, and operational workflows where reliability, clarity, and offline/real\-world constraints matter. You will spend the bulk of your time in Flutter and Dart, building the applications at the core of our product, while working as a comfortable full\-stack engineer across the rest of the stack. That means collaborating closely with backend engineers on the shared REST and GraphQL APIs our mobile and web clients depend on, and helping shape the architecture and contracts behind them as we invest in that layer. You set a strong architectural direction and you stay in the code.



This role suits a product\-minded engineer who can move quickly from a rough idea to a working prototype alongside product and design, then carry that prototype through to a sound, well\-architected feature with cross\-platform impact and the end user in mind. You should be experienced with agentic, AI\-assisted development and confident directing it; our team uses Claude Code, Codex, skills, and MCP integrations every day for building, support, and documentation. We are looking for someone who can help the team innovate with these tools while grounding that work in engineering experience and proven best practices, including authoring the skills and workflows that make the whole team faster.


**What's the Opportunity**
--------------------------


* Build, test, and ship high\-quality Flutter applications across iOS and Android
* Help shape mobile architecture and establish the patterns and standards the team builds on, while staying hands\-on in the codebase
* Collaborate with backend engineers on shared REST and GraphQL APIs; weigh in on contracts and data\-flow decisions, and go hands\-on with lightweight contributions when the situation calls for it.
* Partner with product and design to prototype ideas rapidly, then turn validated prototypes into durable, maintainable features
* Bring a product engineering mindset and an end\-user focus to every feature, considering cross\-platform impact from the start
* Use and direct AI\-assisted development with Claude Code, skills, and MCP day to day; author skills and workflows that raise the team's velocity and quality
* Work effectively across multiple product areas, maintaining context and technical consistency as mobile priorities evolve
* Contribute to code reviews and to the technical growth and mentorship of the engineers around you
* Support customers and field technicians directly by troubleshooting code and resolving issues end to end, using tools like Sentry and Datadog to trace problems across the stack and drive root cause analysis on the hard ones.

**Qualifications**
------------------


* 5\+ years of software development experience, with strong, demonstrated expertise in Flutter/Dart and comfort working full\-stack across backend services and APIs
* Strong software architecture and design skills, paired with a clear willingness to stay hands\-on in the code
* Demonstrated experience consuming and collaborating on REST and GraphQL APIs, and comfort discussing backend design, data models, and service contracts with backend engineers
* A product engineering mindset: able to prototype quickly with product and design, then deliver a sound, well\-built feature
* Hands\-on experience directing agentic coding tools and using agentic workflows as a force multiplier while maintaining ownership of technical decisions
* Strong debugging and performance\-optimization skills, with hands\-on experience using observability and monitoring tools such as Sentry, Datadog, or similar to diagnose and resolve production issues
* Strong context\-switching skills and the ability to stay effective across several concurrent projects and teams
* Exceptional communication skills, with the ability to lead technical discussions and present to stakeholders
* A track record of mentoring engineers and improving the teams you are part of

**Nice to Have**
----------------


* Experience authoring AI skills, building MCP integrations, or designing agentic development workflows
* AWS experience (AppSync, Lambda, Cognito) with direct backend collaboration
* Backend development experience, particularly with TypeScript services (Hono, Zod, OpenAPI) or comparable stacks
* Expert\-level experience with the BLoC pattern and advanced state management
* Clean Architecture, Domain Driven Design, and similar enterprise\-grade patterns
* Local\-first and offline data experience (Drift, SQLite, or similar)
* Native platform experience (iOS, Android) for platform channel and debugging work
* CI/CD pipeline experience with GitHub Actions, Fastlane, or custom automation
* IoT and Bluetooth integration experience for industrial or manufacturing device connectivity

**What We Offer**
-----------------



AssetWatch is a remote\-first company that puts people at the center of everything we do. We want our team members to thrive; that is why we offer a range of benefits and perks designed to support your well\-being, growth, and work\-life balance.


* Competitive compensation package including stock options
* Flexible work schedule with core hours in the Eastern time zone
* Comprehensive benefits including retirement plan match
* Unlimited PTO
* The opportunity to make a real impact every day in the manufacturing industry
* A close\-knit team environment that balances work and life while crafting exceptional products


We have a distributed team that works remotely across locations in the United States. This is a remote position, with collaboration during Eastern time zone core working hours required.



