in-5468eabdcc7eaf00,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=5468eabdcc7eaf00,https://grnh.se/368u7v925us,Software Development and Integration Engineer,AST SpaceMobile,"Lanham, MD, US",2026-07-21,,,,,,,False,,,,,"AST SpaceMobile is building the first and only global cellular broadband network in space to operate directly with standard, unmodified mobile devices based on our extensive IP and patent portfolio and designed for both commercial and government applications. Our engineers and space scientists are on a mission to eliminate the connectivity gaps faced by today's five billion mobile subscribers and finally bring broadband to the billions who remain unconnected.

**Position Overview**



We are seeking a Software Development and Integration Engineer to support the development, integration, and deployment of software solutions for advanced communications, aerospace, defense, and mission\-critical technology programs. In this role, you will work closely with systems engineers, software developers, and customers to integrate software components into cohesive, high\-performance systems that meet operational and technical requirements.



The ideal candidate has experience with software integration, automation, DevOps practices, and software\-hardware integration. This individual will play a key role in developing integration strategies, maintaining build and deployment environments, troubleshooting complex technical issues, and supporting system\-level testing and verification activities.


**Key Responsibilities**


* Collaborate with customers, systems engineers, and software development teams to define software requirements, architecture concepts, integration strategies, and test plans.
* Perform integration of software components, firmware, embedded applications, and third\-party libraries into operational systems.
* Develop and maintain software integration plans, procedures, and automated deployment processes.
* Design and implement automation scripts to improve build, testing, deployment, and release workflows.
* Define and maintain software interfaces, integration dependencies, and configuration requirements.
* Configure, manage, and maintain software development and integration environments, including source control repositories, build systems, and CI/CD pipelines.
* Troubleshoot and resolve software integration issues through root cause analysis and cross\-functional collaboration.
* Support software verification, validation, and system\-level testing activities.
* Maintain software build documentation, release records, and configuration management artifacts to ensure traceability and repeatability.
* Support software\-hardware integration efforts and assist in validating system functionality and performance.
* Participate in design reviews, technical discussions, and continuous improvement initiatives.
* Contribute to the development of new capabilities and enhancements for customer\-focused solutions.


**Qualifications**


**Education**



Bachelor's degree in Computer Engineering, Software Engineering, Computer Science, Electrical Engineering, or a related technical discipline.



Relevant technical certifications are a plus.


**Experience**


* A minimum of 5 years of experience in software integration, software engineering, DevOps, or related technical roles.
* Experience supporting complex software development and integration projects.
* Experience working in aerospace, defense, telecommunications, embedded systems, or other highly regulated technical environments.
* Experience with software build, release, and deployment processes.
* Preferred Qualifications
* Experience with embedded systems, real\-time operating systems (RTOS), or software\-hardware integration.
* Experience supporting mission\-critical, aerospace, telecommunications, or defense\-related systems.
* Experience developing automation frameworks and deployment pipelines.
* Familiarity with systems engineering processes, requirements management, and verification activities.
* Experience integrating third\-party software components and applications.
* Knowledge of software configuration management and release management best practices.
* Experience supporting test automation and continuous integration environments.
* Eligibility to obtain and maintain a government security clearance.


**Soft Skills**


* Strong interpersonal skills with the ability to collaborate effectively across engineering and technical teams.
* Proven ability to work within cross\-functional and multidisciplinary environments.
* Excellent written and verbal communication skills.
* Strong analytical and troubleshooting abilities with a structured approach to problem\-solving.
* Meticulous attention to detail to ensure the accuracy of software builds, documentation, and deliverables.
* Strong organizational and time\-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities.
* Self\-motivated with the ability to work independently and take initiative.
* Adaptability and flexibility in a fast\-paced development environment.
* Commitment to continuous improvement and operational excellence.


**Technology Stack**


* Programming and scripting languages: Python, C/C\+\+, Bash, or equivalent.
* Version control systems: Git or equivalent source code management tools.
* CI/CD and build automation tools: Jenkins, GitLab CI, Azure DevOps, or equivalent.
* Software development and debugging tools.
* Linux\-based development and integration environments.
* Software configuration and release management tools.
* Continuous integration and automated testing frameworks.
* Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook).
* Issue tracking and collaboration platforms.


**Physical Requirements**


* Ability to work in a standard office environment and use a computer for extended periods.
* Ability to review software documentation, system diagrams, technical specifications, and engineering data.
* Ability to participate in meetings, design reviews, and collaborative engineering sessions.
* Ability to perform detailed analysis and troubleshooting of software and system integration issues.
* May occasionally work in laboratory, integration, testing, or operational environments.
* Ability to travel occasionally as required for program support, testing activities, training, or customer engagements.


**Additional Requirements**


* Eligibility to obtain and maintain a U.S. government security clearance.
* U.S. citizenship may be required based on program and contract requirements.


*This job description may not be inclusive to the duties and responsibilities listed. Additional tasks may be assigned to the employee from time to time or the scope of the job may change as needed by business demands**.*


