**What you'll do...**
---------------------

**Role summary:**  

The Senior Manager, Software Engineering leads the execution of platform\-level software and AI/ML systems, ensuring alignment with strategic roadmaps and technical standards. This role oversees scalable infrastructure, DevOps practices, and cloud cost optimization while driving full lifecycle software development across multiple teams. The position requires strong leadership in architectural design, stakeholder collaboration, and operational excellence to deliver high\-quality, reliable solutions. By fostering innovation and continuous improvement, this role advances engineering capabilities and supports business objectives through effective project and team management.

 **About the team:**  

The international last mile engineering team delivers scalable, high\-performance software solutions that enhance customer experience and operational efficiency. Focused on automation and continuous optimization, the team designs, develops, and maintains critical business capabilities with an emphasis on solution design, software development, and DevOps best practices. Collaborating closely, members ensure reliable system performance and measurable growth. This team fosters technical excellence and proactive problem\-solving to meet evolving business needs while upholding high standards of quality and performance in a dynamic environment.

 **What you'll do:**

* Lead platform\-level execution of software and AI/ML systems, ensuring alignment with domain priorities and roadmap milestones.
* Oversee shared infrastructure, tooling, and frameworks to support scalable, secure development.
* Drive full software development lifecycle across multiple teams, championing DevOps architecture and CI/CD practices.
* Implement cloud cost optimization and enhance automation, telemetry, and tooling to improve efficiency.
* Mentor engineers, guide architectural decisions, and promote technical quality and compliance.
* Manage stakeholder relationships to align priorities and unblock progress.
* Establish and track operational metrics to guide continuous improvement and ensure high system availability.

 **What you'll bring:**

* Extensive experience leading platform engineering and software development lifecycle across multiple teams.
* Proven expertise in DevOps architecture, CI/CD practices, and cloud financial management to optimize delivery and costs.
* Strong skills in project and stakeholder management, ensuring alignment with strategic roadmaps and milestone tracking.
* Demonstrated ability to guide architectural reviews and system design for scalable, maintainable, and secure solutions.
* Proficiency in integrating platform technologies and collaborating with cross\-functional teams to deliver innovative products.
* Commitment to mentoring engineers, fostering technical excellence, and promoting continuous improvement.
* Excellent communication skills to manage complex initiatives and build effective partnerships.

  

At Walmart, we offer competitive pay as well as performance\-based bonus awards and other great benefits for a happier mind, body, and wallet. Health benefits include medical, vision and dental coverage. Financial benefits include 401(k), stock purchase and company\-paid life insurance. Paid time off benefits include PTO (including sick leave), parental leave, family care leave, bereavement, jury duty, and voting. Other benefits include short\-term and long\-term disability, company discounts, Military Leave Pay, adoption and surrogacy expense reimbursement, and more.  

  

You will also receive PTO and/or PPTO that can be used for vacation, sick leave, holidays, or other purposes. The amount you receive depends on your job classification and length of employment. It will meet or exceed the requirements of paid sick leave laws, where applicable.  

  

For information about PTO, see https://one.walmart.com/notices.  

  

Live Better U is a Walmart\-paid education benefit program for full\-time and part\-time associates in Walmart and Sam's Club facilities. Programs range from high school completion to bachelor's degrees, including English Language Learning and short\-form certificates. Tuition, books, and fees are completely paid for by Walmart.  

  

Eligibility requirements apply to some benefits and may depend on your job classification and length of employment. Benefits are subject to change and may be subject to a specific plan or program terms.  

  

For information about benefits and eligibility, see One.Walmart.  

  

The annual salary range for this position is $143,000\.00 \- $286,000\.00  

  

