---------------


Are you excited about building high\-performance robotic systems that perceive, learn, and act intelligently? Join our Amazon Robotics team to create innovative robotic workcells that transform how we operate fulfillment centers globally. As a Software Engineer, you'll design and deploy intelligent systems that integrate robotics, computer vision, and machine learning into our operations at scale.
  

  

In this role, you'll work on end\-to\-end software systems that bring robots to life in our fulfillment centers. On any given day, you might partner with hardware engineers and data scientists to design infrastructure that monitors fleet performance across multiple locations. You will design, implement, and launch software services that integrate robots with Fulfillment Center cloud services, detect and respond to automated robotic failures through robust error handling, and develop software that collects and presents metrics from the robotic fleet to identify areas for optimizing performance.
  

  

You'll move between prototyping new capabilities in the lab and supporting wide\-scale deployments in active facilities. You'll participate in code reviews with your teammates, troubleshoot system issues in real time, and contribute to architectural decisions that shape how our robotic systems evolve. Beyond coding, you'll have opportunities to mentor colleagues and share your expertise across the interdisciplinary team.
  

  

Key job responsibilities  

* Design and implement infrastructure software that integrates robotic systems into the Amazon Fulfillment Cloud network, enabling seamless communication between on\-site robots and cloud\-based services
* Build and deploy scalable software systems that enable robots to operate reliably and effectively across multiple fulfillment center locations, supporting both new site launches and ongoing fleet expansion
* Develop and maintain monitoring, fault detection, and simulation systems that ensure robotic fleet reliability and performance at scale—including metrics pipelines, anomaly detection, and automated alerting
* Partner with cross\-functional teams—including roboticists, hardware engineers, data scientists, and operations stakeholders—to integrate all components of the robotic stack into cohesive, production\-ready solutions
* Conduct testing, code reviews, and architectural planning to ensure systems meet reliability, scalability, and operational excellence requirements across the full software lifecycle""

  

A day in the life  

Amazon offers a full range of benefits that support you and eligible family members, including domestic partners. Benefits can vary by location, the number of regularly scheduled hours you work, length of employment, and job status such as seasonal or temporary employment. The benefits that generally apply to regular, full\-time employees include:
  

1\. Medical, Dental, and Vision Coverage
  

2\. Maternity and Parental Leave Options
  

3\. Paid Time Off (PTO)
  

4\. 401(k) Plan
  

  

If you are not sure that every qualification on the list above describes you exactly, we'd still love to hear from you! At Amazon, we value people with unique backgrounds, experiences, and skillsets. If you’re passionate about this role and want to make an impact on a global scale, please apply!
  

  

About the team  

We are building the future of robotics at Amazon, creating systems that combine hardware innovation with sophisticated software. Our team brings together software engineers, roboticists, computer vision specialists, and machine learning experts who collaborate to solve complex problems. We're focused on making robotic systems more intelligent, reliable, and scalable—work that directly impacts how efficiently we serve customers worldwide. You'll join a group that values diverse perspectives and encourages continuous learning. Together, we're working to advance robotic technology in ways that haven't been done before, and we're excited to have you contribute to that mission.**BASIC QUALIFICATIONS**
------------------------

* 5\+ years of programming with at least one software programming language experience
* 5\+ years of non\-internship professional software development experience
* 5\+ years of leading design or architecture (design patterns, reliability and scaling) of new and existing systems experience
* Experience as a mentor, tech lead or leading an engineering team
* Bachelor's degree in computer science or equivalent

**PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS**
----------------------------

* 5\+ years of full software development life cycle, including coding standards, code reviews, source control management, build processes, testing, and operations experience

  

