in-528fefeba5ba0ac3,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=528fefeba5ba0ac3,https://bloomberg.avature.net/careers/JobDetail/Senior-Software-Engineer-The-Deployment-Infrastructure/20951,Senior Software Engineer - The Deployment Infrastructure,Bloomberg,"New York, NY, US",2026-07-21,,direct_data,yearly,160000.0,240000.0,USD,False,,,,"_recruit@bloomberg.net, _recruit@bloomberg.net, _recruit@bloomberg.net","The mission of Application Frameworks at Bloomberg is to deliver a seamless, industry\-aligned, and fully supported application platform that enables a delightful Bloomberg Terminal experience. Every day, thousands of engineers across Bloomberg push updates to the Terminal. But behind the scenes? It’s us, the Terminal Deployment Infrastructure team, making sure all that code reaches the right clients at the right time, with surgical precision.  

  

We don’t just build pipelines, we’ve built a targeting engine for software delivery. It lets us roll out changes to specific users or firms with precise dependency control, and rewind any part of a complex chain without rebuilds or redeploys. Need to patch a component in a shared library stack? Easy. Want to A/B test a new UI with a few users in Tokyo? Just point and click. Pushing code to production should feel reliable and empowering, not risky.  

  

**What you’ll work on:**
* Distributed systems spanning Bloomberg data centers and client PCs that update global installs continuously, securely, and silently
* Runtime infrastructure that resolves unique dependency graphs per\-user, in real time
* Full\-stack tools that let thousands of Bloomberg engineers control rollout with pinpoint accuracy
* Solving hard problems around dependency management, rollback, versioning, and real\-time targeting
* Helping define the future of how Bloomberg ships software
  

  

**You’ll need to have:**
* 4\+ years experience in software development using C\+\+
* Experience designing scalable and maintainable distributed systems
* A good knowledge of SDLC best practices
* Enthusiasm to work with stakeholders on product enhancements
  

  

**We’d love to see:**
* Experience with Javascript/Typescript, Go and Python
* Interest in leading impactful cross\-team projects
* A desire to learn and keep up to date with latest technological trends
* Enthusiasm to work with the C\+\+ and JavaScript communities within Bloomberg as well cross\-industry
Salary Range \= 160,000 \- 240,000 USD Annual \+ Benefits \+ Bonus  

  

The referenced salary range is based on the Company's good faith belief at the time of posting. Actual compensation may vary based on factors such as geographic location, work experience, market conditions, education/training and skill level.  

  

  

  

We offer one of the most comprehensive and generous benefits plans available and offer a range of total rewards that may include merit increases, incentive compensation (exempt roles only), paid holidays, paid time off, medical, dental, vision, short and long term disability benefits, 401(k) \+match, life insurance, and various wellness programs, among others. The Company does not provide benefits directly to contingent workers/contractors and interns.
  

Discover what makes Bloomberg unique \- watch our podcast series for an inside look at our culture, values, and the people behind our success.
  
