The Embedded Software Principle is responsible for the architecture, development, and delivery of embedded software systems that power autonomous mobile robots (AMRs) and related robotic platforms. This role leads the design and implementation of real\-time software controlling robot motion, navigation, sensing, communications, safety systems, and hardware integration.  


The Embedded Software Principle serves as the technical authority for embedded systems within the robotics organization and works closely with Robotics, Controls, Electrical, Mechanical, Software Platform, QA, and Product teams to ensure reliable operation in demanding warehouse and industrial environments.  


The ideal candidate combines deep expertise in embedded systems with practical experience deploying and supporting mobile robotic platforms in production environments.  


Key Responsibilities  


Technical Leadership  


Define and maintain the embedded software architecture for robotic platforms.  
Establish engineering standards, coding guidelines, testing requirements, and development processes.  
Lead technical design reviews and architecture discussions.  
Mentor embedded software engineers and provide technical guidance.  
Drive technical decision\-making across robotics and platform initiatives.  
Collaborate with Product Management and Engineering leadership on technology roadmaps.  


Embedded Software Development  


Design, develop, and maintain embedded software running on robotic platforms.  
Develop software for:  
Robot motion control and navigation systems  
Sensor fusion  
Power management  
Communications  
Diagnostics  
Safety systems  
Implement robust and maintainable software using modern engineering practices.  
Optimize software performance for real\-time and resource\-constrained environments.  


Mobile Robotics Systems  


Develop software supporting autonomous robot operation in warehouse and industrial environments.  
Support integration of:  
Lidar systems  
Cameras  
IMUs  
OTA Updates  
Safety sensors  
Motor controllers  
Battery management systems  
Wireless communication systems (4g)  
Collaborate with robotics engineers on navigation and autonomy features.  
Support fleet\-scale deployment and operational reliability.  


Hardware Integration  


Partner with Electrical and Mechanical Engineering teams during hardware development.  
Develop drivers and interfaces for embedded peripherals and custom hardware.  
Participate in board bring\-up and hardware validation activities.  
Diagnose and resolve hardware/software integration issues.  
Support prototype development and production releases.  


Reliability \& Functional Safety  


Design and implement software operating under real\-time constraints.  
Design systems with fault tolerance and graceful degradation capabilities.  
Implement monitoring, diagnostics, and recovery mechanisms.  
Support safety\-related development activities.  
Conduct failure mode analysis and risk assessments.  
Ensure operational robustness in production environments.  


Verification \& Validation  


Define testing strategies for embedded systems.  
Support automated testing and hardware\-in\-the\-loop (HIL) validation.  
Partner with QA and Simulation teams to validate robotic behavior.  
Develop tools to improve testability and diagnostics.  
Participate in release certification activities.  


Required Qualifications  


Bachelor's degree in Computer Engineering, Electrical Engineering, Computer Science, Robotics, or related field.  
8\+ years of embedded software development experience.  
3\+ years of technical leadership or lead engineering experience.  
Experience developing software for mobile robotic systems.  
Strong proficiency in C and C\+\+.  
Experience with embedded Linux systems.  
Experience debugging hardware/software interactions.  
Strong understanding of real\-time systems and concurrency.  
Experience with software architecture and system design.  
Experience working with an RTOS.  


Preferred Qualifications  


Experience with autonomous mobile robots (AMRs).  
Experience in warehouse automation, logistics, industrial automation, or autonomous vehicles.  
Familiarity with navigation, localization, and sensor fusion concepts.  
Experience with safety\-critical or mission\-critical systems.  
Experience supporting deployed robotic fleets.  
Experience working in Agile development environments.  
Experience working with Zephyr RTOS \& OpenWRT",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/The-Home-Depot,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/0b8960c68e5701f4a990dedad687d150,http://www.careers.homedepot.com,"Atlanta, GA","10,000+",more than $10B (USD),We are the world’s largest home improvement retailer. Our scale and resources let us have a huge impact on the world of retail and in local communities.,,,,,,,
