Experience with RTOS environments.  
Experience with Zephyr RTOS and OpenWRT.  
Experience integrating LiDAR, cameras, IMUs, and motor control systems.  
Experience supporting deployed robotic fleets and field operations.  
Experience working in Agile development environments.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/The-Home-Depot,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/0b8960c68e5701f4a990dedad687d150,http://www.careers.homedepot.com,"Atlanta, GA","10,000+",more than $10B (USD),We are the world’s largest home improvement retailer. Our scale and resources let us have a huge impact on the world of retail and in local communities.,,,,,,,
in-9de0ebbdfc330e50,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=9de0ebbdfc330e50,https://alignops.bamboohr.com/careers/126?source=indeed&src=indeed&postedDate=2026-07-21,DevOps Engineer II,,"Indianapolis, IN, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,direct_data,yearly,80000.0,110000.0,USD,False,,,,,"**About AlignOps**  

  

AlignOps is a rapidly growing technology provider that serves the construction industry. We are made up of individuals who share a common commitment to innovation, creativity, integrity, and delivery beyond our customers’ expectations.

  

AlignOps delivers operational tools to scale and grow the construction business. With powerful solutions configurable to meet our customers' unique needs, AlignOps powers construction operations to increase productivity, improve safety, and deliver more profitable projects. As a technology partner, we transform operational data into a strategic asset that provides the visibility and control to make informed decisions that yield tangible results.
  

  

We seek talented individuals who thrive in a dynamic, challenging, and rewarding work environment and emulate humility, drive, transparency, and customer service in everything they do.

 **Job Description**

 **Responsibilities**

  

* Manage and maintain an Amazon\-AWS\-based Linux, Windows, and Docker/container\-based infrastructure, including system configuration, performance tuning, and troubleshooting to ensure optimal system reliability and availability.
* Take a proactive approach to keeping systems operational and anticipating changes required to accommodate growth predicted by trendlines.
* Ensure system and application security, including implementing security best practices, managing access controls, and proactively addressing vulnerabilities.
* Monitor and optimize system performance utilizing monitoring tools to track system health, identify performance bottlenecks, and implement optimizations.
* Monitor database server performance and collaborate with DBAs to maximize database performance as a part of the full infrastructure stack.
* Troubleshoot and resolve complex technical issues, including diagnosing and resolving system failures, network problems, and application errors.
* Collaborate with cross\-functional teams, including development, operations, and security teams, to ensure smooth and efficient infrastructure operations.
* Stay current with industry trends and best practices, including continuous learning and professional development to maintain expertise in Linux system administration, AWS infrastructure administration, and related technologies.
* Coordinate with NVMO/cellular\-connectivity\-providers to establish and maintain connectivity to the AlignOps hosting environments.
* Understand cost models and pricing associated with cloud providers such as AWS and optimize the use of the resources to minimize costs given the performance requirements.
* Other duties as assigned.
  


**Qualifications**

  

* Experience with Linux systems administration, including knowledge of Linux distributions (e.g., Ubuntu, RHEL, RockyLinux, AlmaLinux), shell scripting (e.g., Bash, Python), Version Control Tools (Git / GitHub), system configuration, package management, and troubleshooting.
* Understanding of networking concepts, which encompasses knowledge of TCP/IP, DNS, routing, firewalls, VPNs, and load balancing, as well as experience with network configuration and troubleshooting.
* Experience with and expertise in managing container technologies like Docker.
* Experience with and expertise in managing AWS infrastructure.
* Obtain and maintain the AWS Cloud Practitioner certification.
* Knowledge of security best practices, including an understanding of security principles and implementing security measures like access controls, firewalls, intrusion detection systems, and vulnerability management.
* Proficiency in at least one scripting (e.g., Bash) or programming language (e.g., Python) for developing automation scripts, tools, and applications.
* Capacity to analyze complex problems, troubleshoot issues, and develop effective solutions.
* Strong written and verbal communication skills.
* Strong attention to detail.
* Ability to work effectively with other engineers and stakeholders, including communicating complex concepts to less technically adept audiences.
  


This is a full\-time position located in Indianapolis, IN. Employees hired within a designated radius of the office are expected to work on\-site according to a schedule set by management based on the requirements of their role.

 **Benefits \& Compensation**

  

* The US base salary range for this full\-time position is $80,000\-$110,000\. Our salary ranges are determined by role, level, and location.
* The AlignOps benefit program includes health, dental, and vision coverage. In addition, the company offers disability, life insurance, PTO, and a 401(k) plan.

  



Website: https://alignops.com/about\-us/careers

  


By applying, you agree to the AlignOps Privacy Policy: https://alignops.com/privacy",,,,,,,,,,,,,,,95000.0
in-b7817a3bae39696e,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=b7817a3bae39696e,https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4350071/Beier-Radio-LLC/Automation-Design-Engineer-II-BR?source=Indeed_Feed,Automation Design Engineer II - BR,BEIER INTEGRATED SYSTEMS,"Gray, LA, US",2026-07-21,,,,,,,False,,,,,"Description:
**Summary:**


The Automation Design Engineer is responsible for designing automation and power systems in line with customer specifications and marine industry standards. This role requires efficient and cost\-effective designs, collaboration with procurement and production teams, and a strong focus on quality and accuracy.

**Essential Job Functions:**

* Design and implement moderately complex systems under guidance (e.g., power management, propulsion, alarm/monitoring, steering systems) following all marine industry standards.
* Conduct PLC and HMI programming, system integration, and software testing.
* Collaborate with vendors to ensure equipment design meets specifications.
* Collaborate closely with procurement and production teams to ensure system quality and accuracy.
* Develop, review, and modify project drawings and documentation.
* Provide technical support to service teams and assist in issue resolution.
* Support project documentation (e.g., drawings, manuals, schematics).
* Produce detailed drawings to guide material purchasing, hardware production, and software development for each project.
* Troubleshoot issues and escalate complex problems.
* Develop 3D models to ensure hardware accuracy and facilitate procurement processes.
* Create and distribute comprehensive electrical schematics to the production team.
* Program software for automation systems tailored to specific project needs.


Requirements:
**Competencies:**

* Proficiency in computer\-aided design software, especially AutoCAD and Inventor.
* Proficiency with PLC and HMI programming software, especially Siemens TIA Portal and Beijer Electronics IX Developer.
* Strong understanding of electrical circuitry and electrical calculations.
* Familiarity with up\-to\-date electrical parts and materials necessary for system design.
* Advanced knowledge of marine shipbuilding standards.
* Competence in project management tools and methodologies.
* Ability to work independently and solve intermediate\-level technical challenges.

**Educational \& Experience Requirements:**

* Bachelor’s degree in engineering preferred; certifications preferred (e.g., Siemens, AutoCAD advanced).
* 3–5 years of experience in system design or related roles.
* AutoCAD Certification preferred, not required

**Physical Requirements:**

* Ability to move around within the office setting or travel to attend meetings, conferences, or other business\-related events.
* Occasional field support.
* Prolonged periods sitting at a desk and working on a computer.
* Must be able to lift up to 35 pounds at times.
* Must be able to access various departments of a given location.
* Must be able to effectively communicate with team members, vendors, and other stakeholders, both in person and through digital communication platforms.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Beier-Integrated-Systems,,,,,,,,,,,,,
in-385670174399bc67,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=385670174399bc67,https://block.xyz/careers/jobs/5366105008,"Senior Software Engineer, Ledgering",Block,"New York, NY, US",2026-07-21,,direct_data,yearly,207000.0,326800.0,USD,True,,,,,"Block is one company built from many blocks, all united by the same purpose of economic empowerment. The blocks that form our foundational teams — People, Finance, Counsel, Hardware, Information Security, Platform Infrastructure Engineering, and more — provide support and guidance at the corporate level. They work across business groups and around the globe, spanning time zones and disciplines to develop inclusive People policies, forecast finances, give legal counsel, safeguard systems, nurture new initiatives, and more. Every challenge creates possibilities, and we need different perspectives to see them all. Bring yours to Block.


#### **The Role**



Ledgering is the accounting core that other teams at Block build on. We keep the authoritative records of balances for Square and Cash App, along with the transactions and settlement that move that money. As a Senior Software Engineer on the team, you will build and operate the systems of record for balances and transactions, the settlement orchestration that decides how sellers and customers get paid, and the automated treasury systems that position Block's own cash. At Block's transaction volume, this work has direct, measurable impact on financial accuracy and on the trust merchants and customers place in us.


#### **You Will**


* Design, build, and operate the balance and transaction systems of record that serve as the financial source of truth for millions of merchants and customers.
* Build settlement orchestration that determines how account holders get paid: schedules, amounts, deposit methods, and withholdings.
* Develop self\-serve ledgering APIs with durable semantics and clear contracts, so partner teams can stand up a new balance or transaction type in about a day instead of waiting weeks on custom integration work.
* Emit balance and settlement data that downstream finance, reconciliation, and reporting teams can trust, against agreed data contracts.
* Design and implement reliable, high\-volume distributed transaction\-processing systems, making thoughtful tradeoffs between consistency and availability when both are not possible.
* Drive convergence across a large portfolio of financial services: consistent transaction and balance models, shared workflow tooling, and predictable integration patterns.
* Operate tier\-0 and tier\-1 financial systems against published SLOs, and debug production issues across services and multiple levels of the stack in a high\-reliability environment.
* Work AI\-natively: use AI agents throughout the development lifecycle, and build agents and automation that reduce operational toil across our services.
* Lead complex projects end to end, breaking the work into components and milestones that other engineers can pick up.
* Mentor other engineers and contribute to the technical direction of the team.
* Work with engineers, product managers, and finance and treasury stakeholders across the company to ship new capabilities at scale.

#### **You Have**


* A minimum of 8 years of related experience with a Bachelor's degree; or 6 years and a Master's degree; or a PhD with 3 years experience; or equivalent experience.
* Experience designing and operating distributed, high\-throughput, fault\-tolerant services, with a strong understanding of consistency, idempotency, and failure handling.
* Experience building money\-movement systems such as ledgers, double\-entry accounting, settlement, or treasury, or the curiosity and drive to build deep expertise in the domain.
* Proficiency in at least one major programming language (for example Java, Kotlin, or Go) and strong SQL.
* Experience leading complex, ambiguous projects across multiple engineering teams and driving clear next steps in areas without clear ownership.
* High standards for software architecture and engineering practices, including maintainable and testable code, CI/CD, and observability, in a complex, high\-stakes financial environment.
* Proficiency in using AI tools throughout the software development lifecycle to improve engineering productivity, problem solving, and software delivery.
* Strong written and verbal communication skills.

#### **Technologies We Use and Teach**


* Java, Kotlin, Python
* AI agents and tooling across the development lifecycle, including AMP, Codex, Claude, Goose and MCP
* Temporal, Protocol Buffers, jOOQ, GraphQL
* MySQL, Aurora, Vitess, Databricks, Snowflake
* AWS, Kubernetes, Terraform, Datadog


