in-dd3017f56be5a970,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=dd3017f56be5a970,https://jobs.boeing.com/job/oklahoma-city/entry-level-software-systems-engineer/185/96312245936,Entry Level Software Systems Engineer,Boeing,"Oklahoma City, OK, US",2026-07-21,,direct_data,yearly,70550.0,95450.0,USD,False,,,,,"At Boeing, we innovate and collaborate to make the world a better place. We’re committed to fostering an environment for every teammate that’s welcoming, respectful and inclusive, with great opportunity for professional growth. Find your future with us.


The successful candidate for this **Entry Level Software Systems Engineer** position will join the **B\-2 Software team** located at **Tinker AFB in Oklahoma City, OK** and will focus on supporting the Boeing Defense, Space \& Security (BDS) business organization. The engineer will play a crucial role in designing, developing, testing, and maintaining software system and subsystem engineering models utilizing Jira throughout the end\-to\-end lifecycle that meets industry, customer, and safety standards for the B\-2 bomber program. You will have the opportunity to review, analyze, and translate customer requirements and technical specifications for stakeholder use. The Software Systems Engineer will collaborate with a diverse engineering team to design, develop, and deploy operational flight software used on the B\-2\. Your expertise will be instrumental in developing, maintaining, enhancing, and optimizing system and subsystem components and functionalities within the B\-2 software that fall under Boeing responsibility. Additionally, you will be a system and subsystem resource to team members, who will debug and resolve issues identified to ensure the reliability and efficiency of software products.  

  



**Position Responsibilities:**


* Supporting software development on Agile teams which are tasked with integrating/implementing solutions onto a platform
* Uses analytical problem\-solving skills to assist in the resolution of complex problems
* Uses engineering skills to deliver improved weapon system capabilities to our customers
* Applies engineering knowledge to continuously improve processes and tools
* Applies knowledge of engineering principles to conduct various analyses
* Gathers information to design, develop, analyze, and maintain software systems that meet industry, customer and internal quality, safety, security and certification standards.
* Partners with appropriate stakeholders to communicate system definition and participates in translation of system\-level requirements into software requirements that meet customer, operational, and performance requirements and have clear traceability to design, code, and test artifacts.
* Assists in completion of software system\-level analyses to identify risk, issues, and opportunities; supports integration and deployment of mitigation actions throughout the software lifecycle.
* Participates in code reviews to ensure alignment to requirements and standards.

**Basic Qualifications (Required Skills/Experience):**


* Ability to obtain a Secret U.S. Security clearance (Post\-Start)
* Bachelor's Degree
* This position is located in Oklahoma City, OK. Candidates must be able to relocate if not already living in the local area.
* Ability to travel up to 10% of the year
* Ability to troubleshoot, perform data analysis, and follow implementation instructions

**Preferred Qualifications (Desired Skills/Experience):**

* Bachelor of Science degree from an accredited course of study in engineering, engineering technology (includes manufacturing engineering technology), chemistry, physics, mathematics, data science, or computer science and 0 years of related work experience **OR** Bachelor’s Degree and 4\+ years of directly related work experience **OR** 8\+ years of related, relevant experience
* Experience in handling documentation products for the use of developers and stakeholders, specifically regarding software requirements
* Ability to work effectively in a team environment and communicate with stakeholders of different backgrounds and skill levels
* Experience with software design and development tools such as DOORS and logic diagrams
* Technical writing experience

**Drug Free Workplace:**


Boeing is a Drug Free Workplace where post offer applicants and employees are subject to testing for marijuana, cocaine, opioids, amphetamines, PCP, and alcohol when criteria is met as outlined in our policies.


