in-4a02a9d3b49c54db,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=4a02a9d3b49c54db,https://www.careers.peraton.com/jobs/data-processing-systems-software-operations-engineer-monrovia-california-168910-jobs--engineering--,Data Processing Systems Software Operations Engineer,Peraton,"Monrovia, CA, US",2026-07-21,,direct_data,yearly,66000.0,106000.0,USD,False,,,,,"##### **About Peraton**


Peraton is a next\-generation national security company that drives missions of consequence spanning the globe and extending to the farthest reaches of the galaxy. As the world’s leading mission capability integrator and transformative enterprise IT provider, we deliver trusted, highly differentiated solutions and technologies to protect our nation and allies. Peraton operates at the critical nexus between traditional and nontraditional threats across all domains: land, sea, space, air, and cyberspace. The company serves as a valued partner to essential government agencies and supports every branch of the U.S. armed forces. Each day, our employees solve the most daunting challenges that our customers face. Visit peraton.com to learn how we’re keeping people around the world safe and secure.


##### **Program Overview**


Provide critical communications and tracking for multiple spacecraft from three complexes located globally, and operates year round 24 hours/7days to provide continuous contact with the spacecraft. The program fulfills NASA goals by supporting NASA deep space mission set, including NASA\-funded missions and collaborative international missions.
##### **About The Role**


Peraton is seeking a **Data Processing Systems** **Software Operations Engineer** to support our Deep Space Network (DSN) Operations and Maintenance O\&M contract with the Jet Propulsion Laboratory (JPL) and NASA in Monrovia, CA.

  

The Deep Space Network is NASA’s international array of giant radio antennas that supports interplanetary spacecraft missions, plus a few that orbit Earth. The DSN also provides radar and radio astronomy observations that improve our understanding of the solar system and the larger universe. The antennas of the Deep Space Network are the indispensable link to explorers venturing beyond the moon. They provide the crucial connection for commanding our spacecraft and receiving their never\-before\-seen images and scientific information on Earth, propelling our understanding of the universe, our solar system and ultimately, our place within it.

  

The successful candidate will oversee the lifecycle management of software components used in data processing. The candidate may be responsible for multiple assemblies and must understand their capabilities, performance standards, and limitations.

  

**Responsibilities:**


* Perform acceptance testing and create comprehensive test reports
* Support Project Interface Testing and Demonstrations at DTF\-21 and DSCCs
* Take part in DSN design and readiness reviews
* Review and critique technical procedures for the installation, test and operation of subsystem
  

software components
* Determine test resource requirements and schedule tests to meet project deadlines
* Identify and categorize Software Anomalies (ARs) and work with the CDE toward resolution
* Liaise between station personnel and DSN Development and Operations Services Office (DDOSO) for the resolution of operational problems, failures, and discrepancies
* Monitor, measure, and analyze SPS subsystem functions and performance
* Identify, troubleshoot, and resolve discrepancies, failures, and problems
* Provide real\-time technical support for critical and high\-profile DSN activities and events
* Analyze discrepancy reports (DRs)
* Coordinate with Deep Space Communications Complex (DSCC) personnel and JPL Design Engineering to investigate failures and resolve operational problems
* Maintain technical cognizance of subsystem capabilities, configurations and performance
* Support System Performance Analysis Reporting
* Develop operational processes to prevent, avoid, or work around anomalies that could affect
  

the quantity or quality of data services
* Provide technical guidance to DSCCs in the form of system\-dependent Cognizant OE
  

Advisory/Directives (CAD)
* Lead the effort to mentor less experienced OEs to support the SPS products and services
  
##### **Qualifications**


**Required Qualifications:**


* 2 years with BS/BA; 0 years with MS/MA; 6 years with no degree
* U.S. Citizenship Required
* Must be competent in test theory, test methodologies, software safety, and the fundamentals of computer science and software design.
* Must possess strong organizational and communication skills and be able to effectively manage multiple tasks and priorities to meet deadlines on projects.
* Travel to Jet Propulsion Laboratory and the Goldstone Deep Space Communication Complex (GDSCC) to support customer requirements.
* The ability to undergo a trusted background check and pass a National Criminal Information Check (NCIC).

**Desired Qualifications:**


* Experience with DSN processes governing Test and Transfer
* Fast learner, interested in problem solving, a self\-starter who can make defined requirements from a user's inputs, and be flexible with solutions.
* Experience interfacing successfully across various departmental levels.
* Capacity to adapt to change quickly.
* Analytical skills, detail oriented and ability to multi\-task.
* Good written and oral communication skills.
* Candidate must be able to work in a team environment; proactive; innovative; articulate; able to present briefing material to customers during formal reviews; demonstrate good problem\-solving techniques and skills.
##### **Details**


**Target Salary Range:** $66,000 \- $106,000\. This represents the typical salary range for this position. Salary is determined by various factors, including but not limited to, the scope and responsibilities of the position, the individual’s experience, education, knowledge, skills, and competencies, as well as geographic location and business and contract considerations. Depending on the position, employees may be eligible for overtime, shift differential, and a discretionary bonus in addition to base pay.


**Benefits Statement:** Peraton offers eligible employees a variety of benefits including medical, dental, vision, life, health savings account, short/long term disability, EAP, parental leave, 401(k), paid time off (PTO) for vacation, and company paid holidays. A full listing of available benefits can be viewed at https://www.careers.peraton.com/benefits.


**Application Statements:** The application period for the job is estimated to be 30 days from the job posting date. However, this timeline may be shortened or extended depending on business needs and the availability of qualified candidates. By applying to this job, you are expressing interest in the role and the Company. During the review of your application, you may be required to participate in an on\-camera interview, as well as participate in a process to verify your identity.


**EEO:** Equal opportunity employer, including disability and protected veterans, or other characteristics protected by law.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Peraton,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/a7deaeae4e9e01376ab02161b2008b59,http://www.peraton.com,"Reston, VA","10,000+",$5B to $10B (USD),The future is here and Peraton is building it. We're fearlessly solving the toughest national security challenges and want you to join us.,,,,,,,86000.0
in-15ddf1a25f2cb493,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=15ddf1a25f2cb493,https://pvm.bamboohr.com/careers/160?source=indeed&src=indeed&postedDate=2026-07-21,Mid Level Forward Deployed Engineer,PVM Inc,"Dahlgren, VA, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,True,,,,,"**ON SITE:** Naval Support Facility Dahlgren, VA \- **ACTIVE SECRET CLEARANCE REQUIRED**


**Reports to:** Echo


**Direct reports:** None. Delta’s provide performance feedback on other engineers and participate in company peer mentorship program.


**Travel:** 0\-10%

  


**The Role**



As a **Mid\-Level Forward Deployed Engineer (FDE)**, you will contribute directly to the development and delivery of Palantir capabilities. You will build analytical dashboard features, support CI/CD pipeline tasks, and work within a structured agile environment alongside senior engineers and government stakeholders. You will operate in two\-week sprint cycles, contributing to feature delivery from design through deployment.



At our organization, an FDE takes ownership of their work — building reliable features, writing meaningful code, and ensuring each sprint increment is production\-ready.

 **Key Responsibilities**


* Provide embedded engineering support for the Palantir system, working alongside operational users and senior engineers to deliver mission\-aligned capabilities
* Perform data integration and ontology engineering tasks, including building and maintaining pipelines, implementing metric definitions, and aligning data transformations to the Foundry Ontology to ensure consistent interpretation across the platform
* Develop workflows, applications, dashboards, and AI\-enabled features using Foundry's Workshop/Slate application layer under guidance from senior engineers
* Participate in intake, triage, and solution framing activities — helping translate user needs and stakeholder requests into well\-scoped engineering work
* Contribute to production hardening and transition efforts, including CI/CD pipeline configuration, build scripts, automated tests, and environment promotion workflows to ensure features are deployment\-ready
* Support sustainment and iterative improvement operations by resolving defects, delivering incremental enhancements, and maintaining stable operations across deployed capabilities
* Produce clear technical documentation, including configuration notes, runbooks, and sprint artifacts
* Participate in sprint planning, daily standups, sprint reviews, and demonstrations for government stakeholders
* Conduct testing and validation to confirm workflows, dashboards, and AI features function correctly and that data aligns with approved definitions
* Identify integration issues, surface blockers early, and collaborate with senior engineers to resolve them

 **Preferred Qualifications**


* Hands\-on experience with Palantir Foundry, including pipelines, Workshop/Slate, and Ontology
* 3\+ years of software engineering experience
* Experience with Python, TypeScript, or Java in cloud\-based data platforms
* Experience working in government, defense, or classified environments
* Ability to independently build features, test them, and deliver production\-ready functionality
* Comfortable working in small, fast\-moving technical teams

 **About PVM \& Benefits**



At PVM, we mean it when we say we value diversity. As a PVM team member, you will work with people from all different backgrounds that are passionate about the problems we solve for our customers and are focused on delivering value for our clients. Our culture encourages problem solving, leadership, and innovation, and creates an environment that will support your professional and personal growth. Here are a few highlights of the advantages of being a part of the PVM community:


* Opportunities for growth and advancement
* Tuition/Training reimbursement
* Peer bonus program
* Remote and on\-site positions available
* Unlimited PTO
* Flexible work schedule

  

PVM delivers digital services that help government agencies unlock the power of their data for good and maximize the value of their technology investments. We design, develop, and deploy solutions to solve mission\-critical problems. PVM is a black\- and service\-disabled veteran\-owned small business and was founded by a retired Naval officer out of frustration with the status quo with one goal in mind: to help his fellow Shipmates solve the problems they were facing every day. Today, we continue to be driven by that same goal and are focused on taking on our clients' missions as our own to make a difference in the communities we serve. PVM believes in equal opportunity employment. We won't discriminate against any employee or applicant based on race, gender, nationality, age, religion, disability, military status, or sexual orientation. As a company and as individuals, we're committed to providing an inclusive and welcoming environment for our team, our family members, and our clients.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/Pvm-Inc,,,,,,,,,,,,,
in-188cbdb6657650b5,indeed,https://www.indeed.com/viewjob?jk=188cbdb6657650b5,https://recruiting.paylocity.com/Recruiting/Jobs/Details/4347441/The-National-World-War-II-Museum/Application-Automation-Engineer?source=Indeed_Feed,Application & Automation Engineer,The National WWII Museum,"New Orleans, LA, US",2026-07-21,fulltime,,,,,,False,,,,,"Description:

The National WWII Museum is currently seeking an Application and Automation Engineer. The Application and Automation Engineer is responsible for supporting, maintaining, integrating, and improving the Museum’s business\-critical applications, with primary focus on the Digital Asset Management platform and related workflows, integrations, data flows, reporting, and support processes.


This role partners with IT, business departments, vendors, and project stakeholders to ensure assigned applications are reliable, secure, documented, and supportable. The position combines application administration, troubleshooting, automation, light development, integration support, reporting support, vendor coordination, and process improvement.


This is a hands\-on technical role and does not include people\-management responsibilities.


Requirements:

Digital Asset Management and Business Application Support

* Serve as IT’s primary technical support resource for the Museum’s Digital Asset Management platform and other assigned business applications.
* Support application configuration, workflows, permissions, user access, metadata related processes, reports, and operational support needs.
* Troubleshoot application issues, user access problems, data inconsistencies, integration failures, workflow errors, reporting issues, and user\-reported defects.
* Work with business users to understand support needs and translate them into clear technical actions, vendor requests, configuration changes, or process improvements.
* Help distinguish between business process ownership, vendor responsibility, and IT technical support responsibilities.
* Support application lifecycle activities, including upgrades, patches, configuration changes, access reviews, testing, migrations, and vendor\-supported enhancements.


Integrations, Data Flows, and Automation

* Support and improve integrations between Museum applications, databases, SaaS platforms, reporting tools, file systems, and operational systems.
* Develop, maintain, and troubleshoot automations that reduce manual work, improve consistency, and support business processes.
* Build or support workflows using approved tools such as Microsoft 365, Power Automate, scripts, APIs, scheduled jobs, or vendor\-supported integration tools.
* Troubleshoot failed integrations, broken workflows, data synchronization issues, automation errors, and related system dependencies.
* Ensure automations and integrations are secure, documented, supportable, and not dependent on undocumented individual knowledge.

Reporting and Data Support

* Support operational reporting needs tied to Museum applications, data workflows, and business processes.
* Assist with data extraction, formatting, validation, reconciliation, and basic analysis where appropriate.
* Support Power BI, Excel\-based reporting, application exports, and other approved reporting tools as assigned.
* Help departments improve recurring reports, dashboards, manual data processes, and repeatable reporting workflows.
* Ensure reporting processes are accurate, documented, and repeatable.

Application Security and Access Support

* Support secure access practices for assigned applications, including account provisioning, deprovisioning, role assignments, permissions reviews, and administrative access documentation.
* Partner with Cybersecurity and Infrastructure teams on SSO, MFA, conditional access, service accounts, privileged access, and authentication\-related concerns.
* Ensure application access changes follow approved IT processes and are appropriately documented.
* Identify and escalate risks related to shared accounts, excessive permissions, unsupported integrations, weak authentication, undocumented service accounts, or unclear ownership.

Vendor, Stakeholder, and Operational Coordination

* Open, track, and manage vendor support cases for assigned applications through resolution.
* Coordinate troubleshooting sessions between vendors, IT staff, business users, and project stakeholders.
* Communicate application issue status, risks, dependencies, and resolution progress clearly to affected stakeholders.
* Maintain application support documentation, including configuration notes, integration details, workflow logic, access models, vendor contacts, escalation paths, known issues, dependencies, schedules, credentials ownership, and recovery steps.
* Provide input to IT leadership on recurring application issues, vendor performance, support gaps, lifecycle concerns, and improvement opportunities.
* Support DAM governance and broader application governance efforts by helping clarify technical ownership, escalation paths, and repeatable support processes.
* Perform other duties as assigned.

**Required Qualifications**

* 3\+ years of experience in application support, systems analysis, automation, integration support, software support, or related IT role.
* Experience supporting business applications in a production environment.
* Working knowledge of application configuration, permissions, user access, workflows, data imports/exports, and vendor support processes.
* Experience with automation, scripting, APIs, reporting tools, or low\-code/no\-code workflow tools.
* Ability to troubleshoot application issues across users, data, integrations, permissions, and vendor platforms.
* Strong documentation skills.
* Strong customer service and communication skills.
* Ability to work with both technical teams and non\-technical business users.
* Ability to manage multiple priorities and support requests in a resource\-constrained environment.

**Preferred Qualifications**

* Experience with Digital Asset Management platforms, especially NetX.
* Experience supporting cultural institution, museum, archival, collections, media, or digital content workflows.
* Experience with Microsoft 365, SharePoint, Power Automate, Power BI, SQL, REST APIs, scripting, or workflow automation.
* Familiarity with metadata, digital asset workflows, file movement, content publishing, or media management processes.
* Experience supporting integrations between SaaS platforms, databases, file systems, and reporting tools.

In addition to offering competitive wages, the Museum’s benefits package includes:

* Medical insurance – 2 plan options; Museum pays 75% of premium
* Dental and vision insurance
* Flexible spending account
* 401(k) – Museum matches 50% of employee contribution up to 6%; employer contribution full vested after 3 years of employment
* Life insurance and AD\&D \- $15,000 policy employer paid; additional life and AD\&D available
* Long term disability insurance
* Paid vacation and sick leave, 10 paid holidays per year
* Free parking
* Tuition assistance and professional development
* Employee assistance program


The National WWII Museum is an equal opportunity employer and seeks diversity in its workforce. We are dedicated to a policy of non\-discrimination in employment on any basis including race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws. Consistent with the Americans with Disabilities Act, applicants may request accommodations needed to participate in the application process.",,https://www.indeed.com/cmp/The-National-Wwii-Museum,https://d2q79iu7y748jz.cloudfront.net/s/_squarelogo/256x256/c9ebb061feda410491ef2c3240fe4346,http://www.nationalww2museum.org,New Orleans,201 to 500,,,,,,,,,
